{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5","id":1497012,"title":"Feeding in Classic Vampire versus V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-13T13:25:46-08:00","id":1497012,"title":"Feeding in Classic Vampire versus V5","content":"Feeding is one of the elements of V:TM that was massively overhauled. This is something that is rarely discussed because so many other more controversial elements usually take center stage but I think this is a basic element that needs more attention. So, this is a thread to discuss which type of feeding and how it affects a vampire's night to night unliving is preferable. Also, what were good up and downs for both.<br /> <br /> The changes for the way feeding is conducted:<br /> <br /> * The Hunger Dice makes it much-much harder to &quot;pack&quot; your Blood Pool so that the Hunger never goes away. You are always hungry unless you've killed someone so that the Beast is a constant concern for Hunger frenzies. Classic, however, make it so running out of blood is the much much larger danger.<br /> <br /> * Blood Potency and Generation versus Generation alone.<br /> <br /> * Generation has a FAR vaster affect on the ability for someone to &quot;ethically&quot; feed with Blood Packs and Animal Blood being something that only the Highest Generation Kindred can feed on. This is, of course, a huge change from classic where only the Methuselah's Thirst made it IMPOSSIBLE to feed on animal blood or &quot;cold blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Resonance obviously exists in V5 and is related to your ability to gain Disciplines. Blood is just blood in Classic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-13-2022, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T13:40:27-08:00","id":1497015,"title":"","content":"The hunger dice is a nice concept, helps with reducing bookkeeping and is very thematic, too bad that the way they are implemented leaves a lot to be desired, doesn't matter how you want to put it, punishing players for rolling too well is stupid, at least allow to spend willpower to avoid the effects of a chaotic success or whatever the hell they called it.<br /> <br /> Regarding the feeding limitations, that is one of the things I hate the most, using bloodbags and animal blood has always been a thing and this change only limits players options even more, resonance likewise is an unnecessary addon that almost nobody will use since it takes a lot of timing and preparation to get the right &quot;flavour&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T15:42:15-08:00","id":1497026,"title":"","content":"The switch to hunger is mostly just a step sideways. Hunger dice are a mechanic for a game where you have very few rolls, but every single roll could have massive consequences. I don't think it really gels with V5's other rules, but I like it in theory and especially like that you're always a little bit hungry unless you've gorged yourself. Classic and Requiem probably should have had some kind of mechanic for keeping yourself from being too full but hunger dice needed another revision or three. There's other ways you could do it, like diminishing returns on blood or targets, but such things might require too much bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> As to Blood Potency, urgh. Admittedly most of my issues are due to not thinking it fits <i>thematically</i>, but it's feeding restrictions scale way too rapidly. Requiem BP doesn't hinder animal blood consumption at level 2, and has the vitae gain from blood bags gradually decrease. Plus the need to kill to get hunger below 2 really reduces the practicalities of playing low gen kindred.<br /> <br /> Resonance is a 'how much does this rule actually get used' thing. Like maybe there's tables who make extensive use of such rules, they're not the kind I've tended to play at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T23:02:23-08:00","id":1497072,"title":"","content":"I've thought on it a lot over the last four years, but I think Blood Potency just doesn't work in VTM. It's a neat idea to let PCs have a &quot;level&quot; that increases, like Arete or Dharma, but realistically, it only becomes relevant in games spanning decades or centuries. <br /> <br /> When it does become relevant, the need to balance the advantages it offers against banes and the like makes PCs unplayable at a certain level.<br /> <br /> Plus, if you just allow vampires to spend as much vitae as they want on a single active Discipline use per turn, then the other limitations on vitae don't matter as much.<br /> <br /> Predator Types are a good idea as an optional thing. I don't think they're essential, but they make a nice replacement for freebie points to round out a character a little.<br /> <br /> Resonance as a fluff thing would be fine. I might let it give a minor bonus in extreme cases, but certainly no more than a couple of dice -- and that only if you drink all the target's blood, killing them. However, I think vampires being able to detect different flavours of blood from scent alone would make a good addition to a vampire's core abilities, and adds to the beastliness. (I would also add night sight and VTR2e's Kindred Senses.)<br /> <br /> I quite like MET's optional feeding rules, which use cards with different victims on. You can use that system quite well in any vampire game. Simply arrange all the victims into groups, which becoming hunting locations, and anyone who wants to feed in a given location can choose a card from that location. The victim may just have a flavour, or they may give a small bonus, and the card can also list any complications, items the target holds, and so on.<br /> <br /> In most cases, I would make hunting an interlude or montage. But occasionally it needs to take the focus.<br /> <br /> Hunger is a neat idea, but the execution isn't quite how I'd do it. Hunger as a *bonus* on certain rolls makes sense. You could use it to replace dice only where you are trying to concentrate despite gnawing hunger or if you are at risk of frenzy.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think the last part of the puzzle is the Beast itself. If everyone had a Beast Nature, you could rule that certain conditions make it ascendant, making your Human Nature dormant. At that point, the only way to regain Willpower would be via playing your Beast Nature, and your Human Nature would only reassert itself when your blood pool is completely filled again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T23:15:12-08:00","id":1497073,"title":"","content":"Its a difference of game experience for me I think the hunger system when combined other mechanics simulates childer/ mid neonate life very well: you're twitchy and don't have a great handle on your thirst. In contrast the blood pool combined with raw power of a non v5 vampire simulates mid neonate+, you have a good grasp on your beast but frenzies are more destructive in the same sense a rabid rottweiler is worse than a chiwawa. <br /> <br /> Couple of minor points<br /> <br /> -generation pre 5 can be frustrating to play with and was pretty messy In terms of disciplines.<br /> <br /> -the v5 hunger system feels incomplete somehow as though it needed more time in development.<br /> <br /> -resonance is pointless filer <br /> <br /> -despite v5s best efforts you will get bored with feeding eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-15-2022, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T12:21:57-08:00","id":1497108,"title":"","content":"Hunger in V5 simply isn't versatile enough for what I want to do with vampires, and it feels completely at odds with the core ideas of Vampire the <b>Masquerade</b>. It's great for pre-20th century horror one-shots where you've suddenly turned, but the horror gets stale and even contemptible after long enough; the system is not suited for vampires who aren't fledglings, and more importantly for modern nights it's just far too problematic to reasonably posit the idea that a semi-competent vampire conspiracy upholds some kind of<b> masquerade</b> with any measure of success when they're getting messy criticals all the time and can't do anything other than avoid doing things to mitigate that. &quot;A Beast I am Lest the Beast I Become&quot; simply doesn't work for V5 because the Beast is always there and controlling it is futile. People are quick to desensitize themselves to the horror when not only &quot;the beast made me do it&quot; is a real thing but they couldn't have reasonably stopped the beast from making them do it. In prior editions, you could lose control and frenzy, but you could do a lot to minimize the chance of that happening and thus you were responsible for your frenzies. You aren't responsible for your messy crits. The only option to not-have messy crits is unreasonable. The best way to play being not-to-do-anything-that-requires-a-roll is shit, quite frankly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pre 5 feeding was<br /> better for the setting because the masquerade was more sustainable.<br /> Better for smart/strategic players because you've got a measurable resource.<br /> Better for players who've put more than an hour into the game, because they're more than likely sick and tired of beastials.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk Generation and Blood Potency, that's an even bigger blunder on the part of V5.<br /> V5's way of doing Generation is in my opinion, moralistic bullshit, and does an absolute disservice to the political cynicism that makes up and inspire VTM's political reality. Generation is a bad trade in V5: You may gain a quick boost in discipline dots, you may gain some extra dice to healing and disciplines, but you're abso-fucking-lutely shooting yourself in the foot by limiting your ability to satiate your hunger. In V5, you have the choice to become a low gen, but it's clearly the choice that will being your character to ruin in morallity, quality of unlife, and I'd argue it even becomes mechanically disadvantageous. Is it really much of a moral quandry when it's nearly objectively wrong to diablerize? No.<br /> Meanwhile, In VTM, you diablerize because there's a glass ceiling and the only way to break it is cannibalistic murder. There are risks, but the only consequence of getting lower gen is being targeted for it, which thematically works wonders. There's a long way to the top if you want to try getting there, and who's to say who's right? Maybe you're being selfish, maybe you'd do more good with that power than the elder you ate (or at least you'll do less bad things, right?).<br /> <br /> Other sideeffects of V5's potency:<br /> 1: Your party is going to be wildly imbalanced by diableries given how much XP you can get from one.<br /> 2: you know for a fact that Methuselah's thirst is not only real but certain, whereas in prior editions it was a distant possibility with little supporting evidence that had people on edge and may have been an issue for a few isolated vampires but for the most part was probably just fearmongering rumours.<br /> <br /> <br /> By almost every metric the games before V5 did hunger significantly better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T17:02:53-08:00","id":1497131,"title":"","content":"Blood potency increases being a mixed blessing at best is not a bug, it's a feature. The dirty little secret of this edition is that you aren't intended to play a vampire, not really. You're intended to play someone with little or no blood potency, but also low bane rating and high humanity, who fights the REAL vampires: the creatures with high power, but also high bane-rating and low humanity. You're supposed to loathe the REAL vampires, and kill them using the subtle advantages of high humanity and low bane-ratings. It's a vampire-hunter game where you are akin to the half turned types like Mina in Dracula and Michael in the Lost Boys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T19:26:20-08:00","id":1497157,"title":"","content":"I think the most interesting thing about the changes to feeding for V5 is the fact that it strongly incentivizes the desire to play a High Generation vampire. From a storytelling standpoint, this has some ups and downs.<br /> <br /> 1. It's a good thing because in &quot;Classic&quot; V:TM, having a High Generation was somehting that virtually everyone avoided like the plague. This actually incentivizes players to try to play 11th, 12th, and 13th generation characters in a way that was never the case before. If you want to be a animal blood drinking &quot;good&quot; vampire, you have to be one of the weaker bloods.<br /> <br /> 2. To further go with 1#, this is something that was actually meant to be the case in 1st Edition that most of the modern vampires were meant to be Thin Bloods and Caitiff and weaker generations. It was the Time of Thin Blood after all. This helps contradict the immense POWER CREEP that was a constant and neverending threat in Classic V:TM.<br /> <br /> 3. It creates some distinct playstyle differences from the &quot;Potent&quot; blood generations and the &quot;Weak&quot; blood with the former being more inclined to be homicidal alien blooded vampires and the latter being more inclined to be friendly neighborhood ones in a way that isn't necessarily wrong from a lore standpoint.<br /> <br /> 4. The fact you can more or less choose your own generation also affects things as it shows what sort of vampire playstyle you have as both have their ups and downs.<br /> <br /> But this gets to the negative:<br /> <br /> 1. SHOULD there be an incentive to play as a high generation &quot;stuffed in a locker&quot; vampire? The thing about being High Generation in previous editions is it SUCKS. You band together in coteries because 4-5 vampires hanging out is less likely to get their ass kicked than one going alone.<br /> <br /> 2. Diablerie is nerfed. Say what you will about cannibalism but the reasons for doing it in previous edition made sense. Whether your ST did the popular house rule of adding a point of Discipline for each kill or not, the rise on a generation was always a good thing. The social consequences might suck but only if you were caught and not if they had a blood hunt on them.<br /> <br /> Combined with all the new Diablerie rules, it seems a lot more hit and miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T22:16:57-08:00","id":1497162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1497131#post1497131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood potency increases being a mixed blessing at best is not a bug, it's a feature. The dirty little secret of this edition is that you aren't intended to play a vampire, not really. You're intended to play someone with little or no blood potency, but also low bane rating and high humanity, who fights the REAL vampires: the creatures with high power, but also high bane-rating and low humanity. You're supposed to loathe the REAL vampires, and kill them using the subtle advantages of high humanity and low bane-ratings. It's a vampire-hunter game where you are akin to the half turned types like Mina in Dracula and Michael in the Lost Boys.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1497157#post1497157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the most interesting thing about the changes to feeding for V5 is the fact that it strongly incentivizes the desire to play a High Generation vampire. From a storytelling standpoint, this has some ups and downs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately I think it boils down to ambition and how you see vampires. In V20, you're most likely a high functioning sociopath encouraged to take risks and murder your way to the top in a gross parody of real world elites. Whether you do so stably or not both serve the cause of satire. In V5 you're a mentally ill minority persecuted from every angle and overcome with guilt, though it's a bit easier to get into politic, it's as CajunKhan says: playing a vampire like a vampire in V5 is a mistake, you're playing a human with issues, and you should be fighting the REAL vampires. The satirical elements are pretty dead in V5. The pre-5 approach is broad and widely applicable and you'll never get bored of it. V5 on the otherhand is overly narrow in scope. I'm (probably) neurotypical, and I find the plight of V5 vampires more difficult to relate too, it feels like it was built for a very narrow and specific audience. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. It's a good thing because in &quot;Classic&quot; V:TM, having a High Generation was somehting that virtually everyone avoided like the plague. This actually incentivizes players to try to play 11th, 12th, and 13th generation characters in a way that was never the case before. If you want to be a animal blood drinking &quot;good&quot; vampire, you have to be one of the weaker bloods. </div> </div> </div> I would argue that some people are attracted to underdogs and would be very happy to start off at a disadvantage. Making them equal or giving them specialness in ThBlAlc... well, you can't be that special underdog anymore (I'd also argue that players flocking to start at 8th gen without consequence is a flaw of prior editions but one that could be remedied) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. To further go with 1#, this is something that was actually meant to be the case in 1st Edition that most of the modern vampires were meant to be Thin Bloods and Caitiff and weaker generations. It was the Time of Thin Blood after all. This helps contradict the immense POWER CREEP that was a constant and neverending threat in Classic V:TM. </div> </div> </div> What powercreep? All I see is well intended design. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. It creates some distinct playstyle differences from the &quot;Potent&quot; blood generations and the &quot;Weak&quot; blood with the former being more inclined to be homicidal alien blooded vampires and the latter being more inclined to be friendly neighborhood ones in a way that isn't necessarily wrong from a lore standpoint. </div> </div> </div> Is this a complaint? It doesn't seem like a complaint. I would argue that lower-gen players being more murderous is more because they wanted an optimized murder character first and picked more gen dots rather than resource dots to support that. Playing a low gen character and then realizing you're really good at murdering happens occasionally but let's not kid ourselves. A similar argument could be made for Tremere and Thaumaturgy: really attractive to powergamers and murderhobos but not inherently problematic. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T03:51:58-08:00","id":1497169,"title":"","content":"One of the core reasons why I didn't like V5 alongside Blood Potency when I first played even though I thought they sounded cool and innovative at first. My opinion didn't change so far and in fact gotten worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T17:22:50-08:00","id":1497240,"title":"","content":"Honestly if the Devs want to outright state in the books that the PCs are supposed to be high generation I don't have an issue with that. I'd like to have the extra BP/turn come a bit earlier, but that would require a rework of how Generation is bought.<br /> <br /> Honestly just abandoning BP and using the chart as a 'how low gen are you' deal probably works fine for the generations PCs are meant to have. It also helps to serve to keep the really low generation kindred out of the direct game, which really was the intention early on. The low gens spend their time in torpor and work via proxies, with the PC's visible enemies being the mid-gens who operate mostly as before.<br /> <br /> Of course this works even better if you rework hunger dice. Probably by having them add to your dice pool during stressful situations and frenzy, while vampires are better able to contain their Beast the majority of the time. Maybe give each character a couple of Beast Triggers, possibly including a Clan one, that cause them to lash out. With enough refinement I think even 4th gen PCs might be playable, even if they have to deal with the difficulty of slaking hunger (which players will still want to do, to throw around more blood buffing and Disciplines).<br /> <br /> Of course at that point you're getting back to the rigid age and generation based structures V5 has intentionally moved away from. Going back to them isn't a bad thing, and would help make the Camarilla more engaging villains, but it's not the current direction of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T07:32:41-08:00","id":1497627,"title":"","content":"My problem with some changes is that they feel really jarring. This was not a thing last edition, but I'm expected to just accept it is now just like that? I'm not going to. I don't dislike V5's mechanics or the atmosphere they create, but it doesn't feel like a natural continuation of VtM because that's definitely not how my characters worked before.<br /> <br /> For the mechanics themselves:<br /> <br /> I actually sometimes prefer the hunger dice to regular frenzy mechanics, though not clarifying that you don't apply them to <i>every single roll</i> came a bit late so many people still think that's how they work.<br /> <br /> Hunger itself is something I'm currently playing around with for V20 purposes. But I have issues with it.<br /> <br /> One, it's way too random. Blood pool makes way more sense to me.<br /> <br /> Killing to get rid of hunger is a very harsh addition to just suddenly throw in now. Feeding restrictions as well. My low gen vampires now need to be roleplayed differently all of a sudden. A compromise I'd maybe go for is to have blood pool and hunger. The blood pool fills and hunger goes down when you feed on any kind of blood, but feeding restrictions dictate what you must feed from to completely shake those last dots of hunger. &quot;Lesser&quot; blood has diminishing returns according to the strength of one's beast/the potency of one's blood. The lower the generation, the more potent the blood, the stronger the curse and the beast, the more it demands the hunt. At the thinnest of blood one can be satiated just by blood components that got separated after a blood donation. Stronger blood needs whole blood. More potent than that and it must come directly from the veins of a living being (animals are still fine), and further potency demands blood taken from a living human. The lowest generations are rumored to have a thirst so terrible it can only be sated by vitae and death.<br /> <br /> Don't like the idea of blood potency. Fits the themes of Requiem, doesn't work for my view of Masquerade's themes. I'd tie potency directly to generation. It dilutes every time you embrace (ie, the childe is a generation higher than the sire) and it's not going up without diablerie. End of.<br /> <br /> Resonance is interesting but too much fuss to bother with mechanically. I'm still not sure if it actually says the only way to increase discipline dots is through resonance or if I'm somehow misreading it and it just gives you a boost, but if I'm reading correctly then that's a horrible idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 11-20-2022, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T00:10:01-08:00","id":1497777,"title":"","content":"My problem with V5 is that it reads like someone's 'clever' set of house rules for a vampire campaign, while there are some brilliant seeming ideas in there, they never seem to have been thought through all the way, because, during the course of the campaign that never becomes a problem. However, when those house rules are then applied to all manner of different campaigns, they turn out to be rather poorly implemented.<br /> <br /> In comparison with the V20 ruleset V5 comes off poorly because V20 has been written to be played in multiple different ways, whereas V5 seems to have gone back to the 90s with its attitude to 'wrongfun'.<br /> <br /> While I don't play much D&amp;D one of the things they get right is that they playtest extensively, so that the rules apply well in all manner of game styles. V5 feels like it was knocked out by copying someone's campaign notes and calling it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T10:21:53-08:00","id":1497812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5#post1497012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding is one of the elements of V:TM that was massively overhauled. This is something that is rarely discussed because so many other more controversial elements usually take center stage but I think this is a basic element that needs more attention. So, this is a thread to discuss which type of feeding and how it affects a vampire's night to night unliving is preferable. Also, what were good up and downs for both.<br /> <br /> * Resonance obviously exists in V5 and is related to your ability to gain Disciplines. Blood is just blood in Classic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do recall that in various V:tM books there are hints, implications, descriptions, and tales about various properties of Vitae. There are also tales, descriptions, and even some rules in regard to blood of various Nightfolk (Mages, Garou, and possibly other types of Supernatural Persons). I think in some books there should be at some information and descriptions in regard to uses and benfits of blood taken from mortals. Possibly the more overall books like Guides, Companions, overall WoD setting books, and maybe also of course some City by Night books as well, have this kind of descriptions or at least some implications and hints. Thus I think that V5's Feeding Resonance rules are actually not a completely new element introduced to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T17:26:04-08:00","id":1497958,"title":"","content":"I am surprise that all of you think the resonance thing as an Afterthought, personally I hate it with all my being and I went back and forth multiple time with my players about how to limit abuse. My player would totally go out of their way to hunt specific human to gain specific bonus which are in my opinion way too strong. Like eating a homeless person and getting a ghost point in obfuscate I get the theme and reason but I truly hate it. <br /> <br /> I understand this is a game and its magic, but I feel there has to be a sort of line of logic here. So going back from earlier edition it was hinted at that drinking blood from homeless people and the sick and malnourish was not as sustaining for vampire than other healthier human. Also animal blood was even worse. In revised hinting that even drinking a cow wouldn't be enough to fill you up (less than 10 points worth of blood). In revised it was hinted at that drinking werewolf blood could potentially give a powerful temporary bonus and have to roll frenzy. It was also the case about Elder Blood and even I can't recall where but Elder Blood in a blood bag preserve was like some powerful stuff. In the source material, If I recall properly there was also some possibility of gaining something from drinking Changeling blood. We also know that drinking Vampire blood also heals people sustain their age(for human) and gives them potence (or Sometimes Celerity or Fortitude). <br /> <br /> Ironically Diablerie has been nerf as well. The person being drain can make a roll and if they succeed the diablerist gains nothing. <br /> <br /> I feel there has to be a proportianal risk &amp; reward here. Animal 1, Human 2 vampire 3 Elder Vampire 4 in scale of giving power by drinking blood.<br /> <br /> I was thinking maybe when drinking you are considered under the effect of blood surge for the remaining of the scene. My players and I were also considering a possible bonus that can only be gain once or twice per session that if a human is healthy that he might give 1 or 2 free xp point that can only be spent in a skill or attribute that is related to the strongest of the victim (for example if the victim strongest dice pool is mental/knowlegde base then the XP can only be use to increase Mental atttributes or Skills. Like they are absorbing a bit of the essence of that mortal. WE are testing it. Also I plan to change the rule for Diablerie, I think the reward or not strong enough. Also the diablerist should be tainted for ever not just a few month or years. Maybe there could be a ritual to hide or at a higher level remove that color from your aura permanently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T10:47:22-08:00","id":1498457,"title":"","content":"To really make &quot;Blood Potency&quot; work in VtM, it needs to be rebalanced with &quot;Generation&quot; reworked to match. I have house rules from the days of Requiem where we used BP, and Generation set your starting BP (under the idea that a powerful sire gets you a more powerful start), and set the upper cap of BP (which goes up naturally for every 1K years of unlife, harkening back to the original methuselah concept). My group thought this gave a &quot;best of both worlds&quot; approach of both not making Generation the end-all-be-all for Vampires, as well as expanding on what exactly Diablerie could do in the moment. <br /> <br /> As for Hunger Dice, I'm split. I like the idea in concept but like others, its execution in practice leaves something to be desired. Around the same time we tried out house-ruling BP, we added a more complex hunger system that was, in retrospect, more than a little fiddly and still needed book-keeping. The desire was to put more emphasis on the act of feeding itself, with hunger and humanity influencing your ability to control how you feed. I'd have to dig up the old .doc file, but it was basically along the lines of &quot;feed frequently to avoid Hunger, but increased risk of being unable to stop when you want and risk feeding frenzies and masquerade breeches.&quot; It encouraged my players to keep a more RP-ish eye on feeding as something more than just &quot;filling up the tank&quot; for their super-powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T21:36:46-08:00","id":1498494,"title":"","content":"The routine feeding of the bloodpool does have its charms. It's a lot more streamlined-something which v5 is supposed to be and their is a creepy subtext of the routine to it. I recently had a pretty cool in game moment where my lasombra get annoyed and then depressed because one of her herd tried to engage with her as a person, the blood pool locks you into the nasty routine aspects of an older vampire than the twitchy childer vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-01-2022, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T01:49:14-08:00","id":1498513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1497627#post1497627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually sometimes prefer the hunger dice to regular frenzy mechanics, though not clarifying that you don't apply them to <i>every single roll</i> came a bit late so many people still think that's how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page reference for that? Because I think many people would prefer that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunger itself is something I'm currently playing around with for V20 purposes. But I have issues with it. </div> </div> </div>Same, really. I like the idea, just not the execution. And I don't like that Hunger Dice actually require you to roll a lot more in some cases (where you'd previously spend blood as a reflexive action) while making you avoid rolling in others (such as where you take a conscious action). That seems the wrong way around.<br /> <br /> I've played around with Hunger Conditions, Hunger Levels (making the blood pool more like the health track with penalties at each level), Hunger Dice on their own, blood pool with Hunger Dice at certain thresholds, and so on. Hunger Conditions work well, especially if you tie bonuses to them. Hunger Dice less so.<br /> <br /> You can roll your blood pool for things, to make it more active. But it only really feels dangerous below five dice, so I gave up on that. Maybe you could remove the WP track altogether and use current blood pool to resist things, but that would require some work. I kind of like the idea of current blood serving as a measure of restraint and composure, but that would probably lead to people topping off their vitae more frequently to keep their &quot;WP&quot; up. And then everyone would have ~8-10 WP all the time.<br /> <br /> So I keep coming back to the idea that Hunger just doesn't work in isolation and that what you need is a system that reflects the Beast, in all its aspects, and not just Hunger.<br /> <br /> So, perhaps use something like the VTR2e model: when you succeed in resisting frenzy, you get a Condition like Gluttonous (Hunger Frenzy triggers), Monstrous (Rage Frenzy triggers) or Animalistic (Fear Frenzy triggers). Only if you score 5+ successes do you avoid that. Failure results in frenzy as usual.<br /> <br /> In some cases (e.g., low difficulty triggers), you could simply take the Condition instead of rolling. There's less risk of frenzy, but you have to roleplay the Beast as a trade-off.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you succeed on a degeneration roll, you might gain a Condition like Guilty (Conscience) or Ashamed (Conviction) unless you score 5+ successes. Failure might trigger the Callous Condition for a scene, as your Humanity slips for a moment.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Beast is less of a binary on/off thing, and more of a spectrum of behaviour that rarely gets switched entirely on or off. And the more triggers you hit, the more these Conditions stack, resulting in a big explosion if you don't release the pressure, but being less frequent and less random than Hunger Dice.<br /> <br /> Or, as I mentioned before, you could replace all those Conditions with a Beast Nature that emerges in different situations, with different resolution conditions based on the trigger. Your Beast Nature thus becomes dominant in play, and you can't regain WP or restore your Human Nature until you give in just enough to satisfy its needs. <br /> <br /> The different resolution conditions would be tailored for your Beast Nature. The Barbarian maybe resolves Rage Frenzy triggers when it dominates or humiliates a rival of equal or greater strength. Maybe it resolves Hunger Frenzy triggers when it gluts more than twice its blood pool in a single scene. Maybe it resolves Fear Frenzy triggers when it punishes anyone who saw its moment of weakness. <br /> <br /> Each Beast Nature might also have one additional trigger that's unique to it -- so, for the Barbarian, it might be being shown up as stupid or weak, because it threatens your desire for control through might. For the Demon, it might be seeing innocence being defended, because that insults your inner need to corrupt and pervert. For the Bandit, it may be seeing others prosper because of something you don't have. And so on.<br /> <br /> I picture the format being like Archetypes with a few extra bits added, so:<br /> <br /> Barbarian<br /> The Barbarian embodies rage, &quot;might is right&quot; and &quot;the law of the jungle&quot;. In life, you were likely passionate but perhaps a little conceited, and competitive but occasionally a sore loser. Now, those flaws have been warped by your Hunger to become something far worse. When gripped by your Beast Nature, you attempt to assert control via force of will and flesh, and break those who would defy you. You do not suffer fools and despise weakness, and eschew subtlety for gross displays of your prowess. <br /> Rage: When enraged, you seek to dominate and humiliate others. You may defeat a target who displays equal or greater prowess in your Primary Attribute category, or humiliate a target who commands authority and respect above your own.<br /> Hunger: When tempted, you attempt to gorge yourself or satisfy your desires. Find a vessel and consume them whole. Keep drinking until your blood pool is full.<br /> Fear: When afraid, you seek to make others even more afraid than you are. No witnesses should be allowed to think of you as vulnerable.<br /> Special: You despise being shown as weak in any area. This counts as an additional rage frenzy trigger (difficulty 6). You will respond by punishing the person who reveals your vulnerability, or else by asserting your dominance over a target who is strong where you are weak.<br /> <br /> (Needs work, but you get the idea.)<br /> <br /> You could also add incentives like VTR2e's system of beats, so that players choose to roleplay the Beast in little increments along the way. Maybe you can retroactively add (10-Humanity) dice to a failed roll to try and succeed via the strength of the Beast, at the cost of flipping to your Beast Nature for a number of turns. This would be the alternative to a Messy Critical, and entirely optional.<br /> <br /> You could also replace Blood Surge/the Quickening with a single bonus of +(10-Humanity) dice, with those bonus dice causing your Beast Nature to assert itself for one turn for every 1 rolled on one of those dice. <br /> <br /> Or maybe the 1s imbalance your Willpower (like in C20), so you circle one WP point (starting with the leftmost uncircled box) for every 1 rolled, and when you spend the WP point associated with that box, you face another frenzy trigger. <br /> <br /> When you resolve a frenzy trigger according to your Beast Nature, you remove the rightmost circle from around that box. When you frenzy, you lose all of them (and refresh your WP?).<br /> <br /> These are just random thoughts, but I think this shows that there are other ways to do this that don't rely entirely on dice rolls. <br /> <br /> Ideally, players should *want* to play their dark sides a little bit, rather than feeling forced by randomness to derail the game. You do that by making the experience fun/a guilty pleasure, and giving the PCs more control over how that dark side presents itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-01-2022, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T08:05:38-08:00","id":1498678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1498513#post1498513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a page reference for that? Because I think many people would prefer that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Directly to hand, not at the moment. I seem to recall the pdf whose name I don't recall that introduced the Ravnos, Tzimisce and Salubri and rules for mortals and ghouls having rule revisions in the back one of which was &quot;yeah, applying hunger dice to literally every roll is a bad idea and we shouldn't have let that be implied. Oopsie daisy.&quot; I don't remember whether that was meant to be a fix applied in hindsight or if they just didn't specify in the core.<br /> -<br /> <br /> When I consider adding something like hunger, I usually look to KotE rather than VtR. The Po and Shadow Soul I particularly love, sort of like your idea for Beast Natures. (I also love the idea of a damned soul clawing their way out of hell and into their corpse, but alas, that would probably heavily derail VtM.) I also considered giving vampires &quot;vices&quot; to go with the virtues, reflecting how their own flaws feeds into their beast. Ultimately homebrewing is such a lot of fiddling though, I never really know what to do.<br /> I definitely agree that when it comes to empowering the Beast outside of frenzy there should be an element of autonomy and enjoyment/power in it rather than random derailment. The corruptive nature of power and such is an element of VtM, after all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T18:52:44-08:00","id":1498720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1498678#post1498678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Directly to hand, not at the moment. I seem to recall the pdf whose name I don't recall that introduced the Ravnos, Tzimisce and Salubri and rules for mortals and ghouls having rule revisions in the back one of which was &amp;quot;yeah, applying hunger dice to literally every roll is a bad idea and we shouldn't have let that be implied. Oopsie daisy.&amp;quot; I don't remember whether that was meant to be a fix applied in hindsight or if they just didn't specify in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so that's the V5 Companion. Checking that book again, the errata section suggests that STs keep the Difficulty secret and let players Talk Half more often (or that STs let them take Automatic Wins) as this was, they say, how V5's playtest cycle ran. <br /> <br /> They suggest this gives players more control over Hunger, but it doesn't really change much from the core rulebook, except encouraging Take Half as a way to avoid the rules. But it does seem that this was how they always intended the rules to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I consider adding something like hunger, I usually look to KotE rather than VtR. The Po and Shadow Soul I particularly love, sort of like your idea for Beast Natures. (I also love the idea of a damned soul clawing their way out of hell and into their corpse, but alas, that would probably heavily derail VtM.) I also considered giving vampires &amp;quot;vices&amp;quot; to go with the virtues, reflecting how their own flaws feeds into their beast. Ultimately homebrewing is such a lot of fiddling though, I never really know what to do.<br /> I definitely agree that when it comes to empowering the Beast outside of frenzy there should be an element of autonomy and enjoyment/power in it rather than random derailment. The corruptive nature of power and such is an element of VtM, after all </div> </div> </div>Yeah, KotE was one of my influences. I love KotE, but VTM needs something slightly different. The Beast is less intelligent than the P'o, and is more primal, but the idea of giving players ways to roleplay the Beast better is appealing to me.<br /> <br /> The problem with homebrew is always that, in isolation, there's so much choice. You could do anything. It's easier to narrow things down with discussion and outside input, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T18:16:40-08:00","id":1499704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1497131#post1497131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood potency increases being a mixed blessing at best is not a bug, it's a feature. The dirty little secret of this edition is that you aren't intended to play a vampire, not really. You're intended to play someone with little or no blood potency, but also low bane rating and high humanity, who fights the REAL vampires: the creatures with high power, but also high bane-rating and low humanity. You're supposed to loathe the REAL vampires, and kill them using the subtle advantages of high humanity and low bane-ratings. It's a vampire-hunter game where you are akin to the half turned types like Mina in Dracula and Michael in the Lost Boys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this perfectly encapsulates everything I have wrong with V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25047-fuzzball6846","name":"fuzzball6846","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T19:31:41-08:00","id":1499713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1497131#post1497131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood potency increases being a mixed blessing at best is not a bug, it's a feature. The dirty little secret of this edition is that you aren't intended to play a vampire, not really. You're intended to play someone with little or no blood potency, but also low bane rating and high humanity, who fights the REAL vampires: the creatures with high power, but also high bane-rating and low humanity. You're supposed to loathe the REAL vampires, and kill them using the subtle advantages of high humanity and low bane-ratings. It's a vampire-hunter game where you are akin to the half turned types like Mina in Dracula and Michael in the Lost Boys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that describing Neonates versus Elders?<br /> <br /> I.e. The Premise of the Game?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T03:38:17-08:00","id":1499733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499713#post1499713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that describing Neonates versus Elders?<br /> <br /> I.e. The Premise of the Game?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because the idea in classic VtM was that you\u2019d hunt and probably diablerize the more potent vampires to gain their nothing-but-upsides strength.<br /> <br /> Now you don\u2019t want to diablerize them because it will make your unlife worse. More, V5 even includes statements that thinbloods could fairly easily become mortal again. Kill your sire and become mortal is a classic vampire trope, yes. It\u2019s just not a VtM one (at least before V5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T08:19:01-08:00","id":1499756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499733#post1499733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 even includes statements that thinbloods could fairly easily become mortal again. Kill your sire and become mortal is a classic vampire trope, yes. It\u2019s just not a VtM one (at least before V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not interested in defending the current anti-Sabbat &quot;one true way&quot; stance of the game, but Neonates vs Elders aside, I'm pretty sure the &quot;kill your sire to become human&quot; actually might have roots in 1e, I remember the example fiction through the book had a (non thinblood) guy who killed his sire and lifted the curse. (I could be wrong, my memory isn't the best.) As I recall, 1e was a strange and magical place where you could be turned into a vampire with a serum, get blood bonded to a vampire by feeding on their ghoul, and the Sabbat could brainwash you by burying you alive. It might've been mentioned as a rumor in other editions, but they largely dropped it in later editions then brought it back for fifth. I'm not so keen on the idea, personally, but it might've been an early thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 12-15-2022, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T09:42:01-08:00","id":1499760,"title":"","content":"The history of VTM kind of reminds me of the history of Monopoly. When Monopoly was first created, it had two rule sets. One was much like the current game, where you try to unironically play a capitalist seeking to horde all the wealth. The other rule set was one in which you basically went socialist and everyone benefited. The idea was that you would play the capitalist version, decide it sucked, and then play the socialist one forever. It was basically an educational tool.<br /> <br /> There was one problem: no one played the socialist version. Everyone preferred to unironically play a greedy capitalist. Soon even the option to play the socialist version was dropped, because it was a waste of space in the box.<br /> <br /> VTM feels similar. The first edition was really a game about vampire-hunters cursed to be vampires seeking to become human again by killing the vampires who had cursed them. Except almost no one played it like that. Most players wanted to unironically enjoy playing vampires. They wanted to hold fancy parties where they dressed up the latest fashions and drank blood out of wineglasses. They wanted to leap across rooftops with their superhuman strength. They wanted to fly through the sky as bats.<br /> <br /> The game adapted to this, created options for players who wanted to unironically play vampires, and not humans laboring under a curse they would soon lift by killing their sires.<br /> <br /> This edition feels like an angry rejection of that adaptation. It's as if the makers of Monopoly twisted your arm behind your back, and shouted, &quot;DAMMIT, YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED TO LIKE THE UNIRONICALLY CAPITALIST RULE SET! THAT RULE SET IS ONLY IN THE GAME FOR YOU TO HATE! YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO PLAY THAT ONCE, THEN SWITCH TO SOCIALISM FOREVER!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's as if the latest makers of Monopoly were so mad that you weren't following the original intent of the game, that they removed the unironically capitalist rule set from the game, only included the socialist version from a hundred years ago, and even deliberately included special mechanics just to make it hard for players to even houserule the unironically capitalist version of the game back into existence. Just twisting the arms of Monopoly players behind their back as hard as they can while shouting, &quot;PLAY SOCIALISTS! LOVE SOCIALISTS! GOD DAMN YOU TO HELL LOVE PLAYING SOCIALISTS! AAARRRRRGH!!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T12:47:19-08:00","id":1499775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499760#post1499760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history of VTM kind of reminds me of the history of Monopoly. When Monopoly was first created, it had two rule sets. One was much like the current game, where you try to unironically play a capitalist seeking to horde all the wealth. The other rule set was one in which you basically went socialist and everyone benefited. The idea was that you would play the capitalist version, decide it sucked, and then play the socialist one forever. It was basically an educational tool.<br /> <br /> There was one problem: no one played the socialist version. Everyone preferred to unironically play a greedy capitalist. Soon even the option to play the socialist version was dropped, because it was a waste of space in the box.<br /> <br /> VTM feels similar. The first edition was really a game about vampire-hunters cursed to be vampires seeking to become human again by killing the vampires who had cursed them. Except almost no one played it like that. Most players wanted to unironically enjoy playing vampires. They wanted to hold fancy parties where they dressed up the latest fashions and drank blood out of wineglasses. They wanted to leap across rooftops with their superhuman strength. They wanted to fly through the sky as bats.<br /> <br /> The game adapted to this, created options for players who wanted to unironically play vampires, and not humans laboring under a curse they would soon lift by killing their sires.<br /> <br /> This edition feels like an angry rejection of that adaptation. It's as if the makers of Monopoly twisted your arm behind your back, and shouted, &quot;DAMMIT, YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED TO LIKE THE UNIRONICALLY CAPITALIST RULE SET! THAT RULE SET IS ONLY IN THE GAME FOR YOU TO HATE! YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO PLAY THAT ONCE, THEN SWITCH TO SOCIALISM FOREVER!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's as if the latest makers of Monopoly were so mad that you weren't following the original intent of the game, that they removed the unironically capitalist rule set from the game, only included the socialist version from a hundred years ago, and even deliberately included special mechanics just to make it hard for players to even houserule the unironically capitalist version of the game back into existence. Just twisting the arms of Monopoly players behind their back as hard as they can while shouting, &quot;PLAY SOCIALISTS! LOVE SOCIALISTS! GOD DAMN YOU TO HELL LOVE PLAYING SOCIALISTS! AAARRRRRGH!!!!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played Vampire: The Masquerade and bluntly have NEVER encountered people who have chosen to play the above way. I've played with about seven or eight separate groups and at least thirty players as well as have encountered many groups. There's been a few Sabbat groups that I've struggled to get more players to involve but even them, the groups always drifted back to the mainstream of Vampire play.<br /> <br /> Which is: <b>Vampires is the melodramatic game of angst and intrigue</b><br /> <br /> Players fucking LOVE to roleplay angst. They love bemoaning the fact they've killed people, the fact they're cursed to be a monster, and the struggle to not kill the innocent. The game THRIVES on the fact the Elders are going to screw you, kill your loved ones, and make your lives living hells. It's a game that has ALWAYS and ALWAYS WILL be about playing the lesser evil.<br /> <br /> No one likes playing a goodie two shoes but I've yet to meet any player who likes being a genuine monster or truly evil for very long.<br /> <br /> It's all about the worse vampires.<br /> <br /> BLOODLINES is basically that sort of playstyle anyway. Keep your humanity up but not TOO up and up against guys like La Croix and the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It's a game about being an antihero.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T12:56:32-08:00","id":1499777,"title":"","content":"I've known a lot of players who ignore the angst and woe. I even made a thread on it. My current pc is slowly reconciling her humanity with her vampiric nature for example. Once she gets an equilibrium then in she'll be a capitalist as the metaphor goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T13:05:27-08:00","id":1499781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499777#post1499777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've known a lot of players who ignore the angst and woe. I even made a thread on it. My current pc is slowly reconciling her humanity with her vampiric nature for example. Once she gets an equilibrium then in she'll be a capitalist as the metaphor goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can ignore the angst and woe.<br /> <br /> But I think you've also been a shitty ST if you don't give the players the OPTION of making the angst and woe there to use as their tool if they want to.<br /> I write vampire fiction in addition to doing vampire games and one of the things I discussed with my horror publishers was the fact that if you portray vampirism as all positives, you are missing like 90% of the fun.<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;woe is me&quot; is fun but you know what is fun? Fucking Spider-Man. And Spider-Man is always getting shit from his supowers. It creates an endless amount of fun for his drama and Spider-Man doesn't have to eat people.<br /> <br /> As a simple tool, you should always have vampirism have MAJOR drawbacks that interfere in your life: The Beast, The Hunger, Sunlight, Rotschrek, or the Masquerade to compensate for your powers. Not because you're FORCING your players to deal with this.<br /> <br /> But that if the players can go off and lament the horror of their condition, they have ample tools for it.<br /> <br /> Vampirism with no drawbacks is silly and uninteresting, IMHO. You can have a vampire, and I've played plenty, who sees it as a good trade off but the limitations are part of the fun.<br /> <br /> If I were to make a comparison, it's like doing a Mobster game where you have no issues of morality or betrayal. You just love being a gangster. Yeah, that's a valid playstyle but there's FUN to be had with the downsides.<br /> <br /> Goodfellas and the Godfather benefit from the downsides.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T13:31:04-08:00","id":1499783,"title":"","content":"You can also go full Hellsing, where yes, Alucard wants to die badly, heavily regrets what he become and would happily accept death at the hand of right people, but well, that doesn't take away from all the positives.<br /> <br /> Or do humor stuff, just because you are playing a vampire doesn't mean you can't have a chronicle based on humor. I once saw a Beast (yeah the infamous Beast the Primordial) game, where they played it like Monsters Inc. (Which makes sense, Monsters Inc is almost like a child-friendly version of the Beast)<br /> <br /> Though I have to say:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499781#post1499781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think &quot;woe is me&quot; is fun but you know what is fun? Fucking Spider-Man. And Spider-Man is always getting shit from his supowers. It creates an endless amount of fun for his drama and Spider-Man doesn't have to eat people.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spider-Man fans have also gotten sick of it. Since Peter <i>never </i>wins and if he does, it will be undone at the start of the new arc. He could be a teenager, middle-aged man, professor or head of his own company and he will still end up in the dumpster after a while. Selling his marriage to the devil, being radioactive and causing cancer, getting cucked by Gwen and these are just a few of the most known ones. (I am not even going to touch Marvel's Mutants, that's another can of worms)<br /> <br /> Some drama and angst is always nice, but I know far too many STs that think drama, personal horror and angst are the only way of playing and will heavily judge people who say otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T14:39:04-08:00","id":1499787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499775#post1499775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one likes playing a goodie two shoes\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>No one you know, perhaps. But around my neck of the woods Vampions is a thing. Worst I\u2019ve ever been able to pull off is \u201cknight in sour armor.\u201d My default is \u201cunironic paladin.\u201d<br /> <br /> I generally need my Dhampir rules when playing VtM with my friends for pretty much that reason. I\u2019ll gladly take the \u201cpower hit\u201d for the \u201cdoesn\u2019t feed on people\u201d bennie. Besides being the party tank is fun (it may not have been intentional, but as written in BJD, the Dhampir is ideal for a \u201ctakes a licking and keeps on ticking\u201d style hunter of the damned).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T17:50:24-08:00","id":1499807,"title":"","content":"IIRC it wasn't even the creator who removed the socialist rules from The Landlord's Game, it was the thieves. It's removal had a political purpose in addition to not being how most people wanted to play (if that's even true, capitalist rules monopoly is a horrible and unfun board game that knocks most players out far too early). The removal of Sabbat play is probably just as much of a Monopoly situation as the swing from an Anarch focus to a Camarilla focus <br /> <br /> But I'll agree that the majority of players probably aren't in it for the angst, or even the hot goths. At the same time they're probably not in it to be conplete monsters, Sabbat/Brood* games tend to be the exception. Most players probably want somewhere between vampire politics and vampions, and some people want to play Vampire for the other big draw.<br /> <br /> Vampires live for a long time. Few other games allow you to pick a historical culture and play through to the modern day. That can be an appealing prospect, and one that shouldn't be overlooked (of course Mages can also nab immortality, but have to deal with Paradox, and Dreaming allows you to do Middle Ages to the modern day with reincarnating Fae souls).<br /> <br /> * 1e Brood, not the 2e Ascended Draugr version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T17:55:57-08:00","id":1499808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499781#post1499781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I think you've also been a shitty ST if you don't give the players the OPTION of making the angst and woe there to use as their tool if they want to.<br /> I write vampire fiction in addition to doing vampire games and one of the things I discussed with my horror publishers was the fact that if you portray vampirism as all positives, you are missing like 90% of the fun.<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;woe is me&quot; is fun but you know what is fun? Fucking Spider-Man. And Spider-Man is always getting shit from his supowers. It creates an endless amount of fun for his drama and Spider-Man doesn't have to eat people.<br /> <br /> As a simple tool, you should always have vampirism have MAJOR drawbacks that interfere in your life: The Beast, The Hunger, Sunlight, Rotschrek, or the Masquerade to compensate for your powers. Not because you're FORCING your players to deal with this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I generally don't like the implication that low-generation vampires (e.g. elders) are more evil because of inherent biological differences with the PCs. It honestly feels a bit too video game-y for my tastes and runs up against the game's themes IMO.<br /> <br /> It should be better, materially, to be a low-gen elder though. Especially if it means trading your soul twice-over. As it stands, I would actively want to become a thin-blood if I lived in WoD, which seems like a bad outcome writing-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25047-fuzzball6846","name":"fuzzball6846","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T18:08:14-08:00","id":1499815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fuzzball6846</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499808#post1499808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't like the implication that low-generation vampires (e.g. elders) are more evil because of inherent biological differences with the PCs. It honestly feels a bit too video game-y for my tastes and runs up against the game's themes IMO.<br /> <br /> It should be better, materially, to be a low-gen elder though. Especially if it means trading your soul twice-over. As it stands, I would actively want to become a thin-blood if I lived in WoD, which seems like a bad outcome writing-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 1st Edition, trying to gain power via diablerie and old age was something you were supposed to want to pursue but with the kind of implications of a gangster movie (I mentioned it before) that if you pursue power and wealth and position in the criminal underworld, it will eventually cost you your soul.<br /> <br /> Same for power in vampire society.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T18:19:12-08:00","id":1499819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499815#post1499815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the 1st Edition, trying to gain power via diablerie and old age was something you were supposed to want to pursue but with the kind of implications of a gangster movie (I mentioned it before) that if you pursue power and wealth and position in the criminal underworld, it will eventually cost you your soul.<br /> <br /> Same for power in vampire society.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's exactly why punishing Diablerie or Generation too much through game mechanics it's a bad a idea. It's the game designers hitting your head with the morality stick. <br /> Instead, Diablerie and Generation should be something mechanically rewarding, so the theme of &quot;what are you willing to do for power?&quot; is present. <br /> What we have now is a &quot;Diablerie is a bad idea, don't do it&quot; theme instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T18:22:19-08:00","id":1499820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499815#post1499815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the 1st Edition, trying to gain power via diablerie and old age was something you were supposed to want to pursue but with the kind of implications of a gangster movie (I mentioned it before) that if you pursue power and wealth and position in the criminal underworld, it will eventually cost you your soul.<br /> <br /> Same for power in vampire society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the conceit is that the cost is the abominable action you chose. As it stands, there's not really a strong incentive to commit diablerie in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25047-fuzzball6846","name":"fuzzball6846","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T21:56:48-08:00","id":1499832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499781#post1499781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think &amp;quot;woe is me&amp;quot; is fun but you know what is fun? Fucking Spider-Man. And Spider-Man is always getting shit from his supowers. It creates an endless amount of fun for his drama and Spider-Man doesn't have to eat people.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I've always found spiderman a miserable unrewarding slog (especially since he divorced his wife in the name of Satan) but I get your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T06:32:05-08:00","id":1499855,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'm always a bit amazed at the variety of experiences we have here when we discuss not just V5 play but also interpretation of V5 as a product, its key aims etc.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">V5 Core, when introducing the concept of the game (pg. 34-36), states that: </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>This is not a roleplaying game where you play good guys. Perhaps your character tries desperately to hold on to vestiges of human morality despite the sordid demands of vampiric existence. Or maybe they have already adjusted their morality to their new condition, telling themselves that they\u2019re no worse than other vampires after they accidentally kill someone.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Whatever the character\u2019s approach to their morality, it\u2019s very likely they end up doing things the player finds morally repugnant. Using this game to explore moral questions and immoral acts can be interesting and emotionally meaningful. After all, the character is not you, and the game is not real. You can use it as a fictional space to explore terrible things, and perhaps even have a little fun with them.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>How long does it take for your neophyte vampire to start getting used to hunting for blood? Do they lie to themselves, insisting that they\u2019re a good person, or do they believe their self-flagellation and guilt somehow makes the killing okay? You can explore these questions through a character and seek out parallels to real-life issues in your own life and the world at large. [...]</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Stories of redemption are within the scope of this game too, but redemption is hard. How do you stay the moral course if you literally have to force your fangs into the neck of a human every night? Other tales exist, with different choices. If your character is a working mother trapped in a vicious, abusive marriage, being Embraced as a vampire can give her power and options she never had before. For the disenfranchised of the world, becoming a bloodsucker is like making a deal with the Devil \u2013 you get a chance to escape the hell you were trapped in, at the cost of your humanity.</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some pages later, when describing Kindred society, the book states that &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>For the first time ever, a neonate can take over a domain if they play the game well enough. What\u2019s more, many of the elders have left their estates, fortunes, and resources essentially abandoned, tended by a few confused blood servants. A sharp neonate can hijack a fortune accumulated over the millennia and use it for their own purposes. [...] It\u2019s a time for a young vampire to make their mark. Why not be like the neonates who spearheaded the capture of Mexico City from the Sabbat? The elders and Justicars of the Camarilla long thought such a bold act impossible. What else might be possible, if you can seize the night first</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">?&quot; (pg. 38).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The premise is still a very broad church, in which Vampirism as a condition can be bemoaned, and redemption pursued, but you can explicitly play it as a power fantasy, or as a descent into monstrosity. In fact, you are explicitly encouraged to test your morality and enjoy your monstrosity, as a metaphor and as an exercise, and </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">redemption is described as very hard, not as the default mode of the game. Nasty politics are still very much the rule of the land here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pg. 337 introduces advice for running games, under the label &quot;Chronicles&quot;: the &quot;Styles of Play&quot; section tells us &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>So, Vampire is a roleplaying game in which joyless monsters wrestle with morality in the shadows of suitably gothic architecture. Right? Well, it can be. But it can be fun too. Past editions described Vampire: The Masquerade as a \u201cGothic-Punk\u201d game. Punk is still as good a word as any to describe the sordid, transgressive joy of playing in a good Vampire game. But Vampire can accommodate many different play styles, and they are all valid, as long as everyone in the game has a good time</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No particular One True Wayism, here: pg. 343 even states that &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The job of a Storyteller or a player is not to morally judge the characters in the game. Vampire works best in a world where everything is in shades of grey and there is a little bit of a sinner in everyone. While the characters can have moral opinions inside the story, you get more play from them if you let them act according to their personalities, motivations, and personal logic</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The section also presents various Campaign modes, such as </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Inheritors of the Illuminati&quot;, &quot;Judgement Night&quot;, &quot;Fun with Evil&quot;, &quot;Hunting Party&quot;, &quot;Fang Gang&quot;, &quot;Nomads&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: again very different chronicle types, which all connect to the various playstiles of traditional Vampire. And playing an Ancilla is one of the default options of the corebook.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunger as a mechanic reinforces a central concept of the game, but nowhere the corebook states or supports the idea that V5 characters should just spend their unlives decrying their transformation and striving to purge the world of more powerful vampires. It also nowhere stresses that the game is best served by one shots, or that characters shouldn't accumulate power and influence. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mechanics here may have unintended or hidden aims here, of course, but I think that V5 gets often misrepresented in its design aims and stylistic choices, should someone judge it by the book (as it will be for most of the new players).</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 12-16-2022, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T09:41:01-08:00","id":1499860,"title":"","content":"I don't doubt V5 had fucked up PCs and darkness in mind, because otherwise there is no way in hell the Setites and the Giovanni would still be around in any form. But 5th edition has also been thrown around like a hot potato in new directions every now and then. The core, and what it was intended to become, may no longer be what it's heading for now. In regards to &quot;the one true way&quot; the game is being designed for, I read it as &quot;you can be a bad guy, but RAW firmly encourages you to play a specific kind of bad guys and not<i> those</i> Bad Guys.&quot;<br /> You're not supposed to play the Second Inquisition because they are the Man and this is Punk. No Alphabet Agencies!<br /> On that note, you're not allowed to be part of any organized hunter group. They are also the Man.<br /> You're not supposed to play a sect that's been a playable part of the game for, what two decades? The Sabbat are comfortable and exalt in their vampirism and That Is Not What This Edition Is About. (Also touchstones must be human, you can not be totally indifferent to humanity or else you will probably wassail. The benefits of high humanity make you more human. Embracing is stains, ghouling is stains, etc. The tenets can be whatever they like, but the levels of humanity are described as though having it high means you're a &quot;good vampire.&quot; There is a strong undertone of intended play which makes the mentions of other themes feel like lip service.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 12-16-2022, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T09:47:53-08:00","id":1499861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499860#post1499860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not supposed to play a sect that's been a playable part of the game for, what two decades? The Sabbat are comfortable and exalt in their vampirism and That Is Not What This Edition Is About. (Also touchstones must be human, you can not be totally indifferent to humanity or else you will probably wassail. The benefits of high humanity make you more human. Embracing is stains, ghouling is stains, etc. The tenets can be whatever they like, but the levels of humanity are described as though having it high means you're a &quot;good vampire.&quot; There is a strong undertone of intended play.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Three decades. I got into VTM about a year after it came out, and my first book was the Sabbat book. I literally owned it before I owned the core.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T11:53:03-08:00","id":1499873,"title":"","content":"The Ministry, Banu Haqim, and Hecata are now all playable fucked-up factions.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's the incredibly fucked up and weird Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are now unplayable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T12:13:34-08:00","id":1499878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499873#post1499873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ministry, Banu Haqim, and Hecata are now all playable fucked-up factions.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's the incredibly fucked up and weird Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are now unplayable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Ur-Shulgi's Path of Blood traditionalists playable? I don't remember.<br /> <br /> I do know that this is why the Sabbat reveal threw me for a loop. Yes, the dynasty of incestuous, necrophiliac enslavers of souls who contain everything from mafioso to nazis, and the cult that encourages you to get people hooked on class A drugs and rape kids to &quot;free yourself from the chains of morality&quot; are a-ok for playing monsters, but the Sabbat and the Society of Leopold? Cancelled!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T12:44:52-08:00","id":1499879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499878#post1499878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are Ur-Shulgi's Path of Blood traditionalists playable? I don't remember.<br /> <br /> I do know that this is why the Sabbat reveal threw me for a loop. Yes, the dynasty of incestuous, necrophiliac enslavers of souls who contain everything from mafioso to nazis, and the cult that encourages you to get people hooked on class A drugs and rape kids to &quot;free yourself from the chains of morality&quot; are a-ok for playing monsters, but the Sabbat and the Society of Leopold? Cancelled!</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem to be a moral judgement, which is interesting. My take on the subject seems to be the idea they want the Sabbat to be STUPID, which is a much different interpretation. The Sabbat are now a bunch of fanatical blood terrorists who don't have much in the way of free will beacuse they're all indoctrinated cultist terrorists who are thrown away like disposable pawns.<br /> <br /> Which is not necessarily WRONG from the way we know terrorists, armies, and cults work but it's a weird line in the sand to draw.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T12:55:08-08:00","id":1499880,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat are only accidentally evil by human standards. They have been classically an example of blue and orange morality, creatures of deep, alien spirituality. I think the Giovanni were kept because they are a very human kind of evil. They are people who can be played up as often having three or four humanity rather than eight in Honorable Accord or Path of the Feral Heart or whathaveyou. The Giovanni are evil in a way that still keeps Humanity central. So they get to stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T12:57:27-08:00","id":1499881,"title":"","content":"The thing with the Sabbat that got them labeled as &quot;not fitting the themes of the edition&quot;, as I understand it, is that they eschew humanity and embrace their vampiric nature. But again <i>they kept the Setites</i>. The other cult that sees their vampirism as the gift of getting the blood of a god in their veins so that they can destroy every semblance of functioning human society to free everybody from the chains of the aeons. Path of Typhon/Path of Sutekh, Path of Ecstasy... they're more invested in the &quot;well-being&quot; of humans than the Sabbat, but not exactly humanity types. They're basically blood sucking snake demons, and they are fine with that.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Hecata, and the Giovanni have the mortal evil and humanity nailed, but the Harbingers? Path of Death and the Soul. Human lives are meaningless and so are emotional attachments, we're just here to study and record the data of your various horrible deaths. Spent a thousand years going insane in purgatory/hell and haven't really been significantly established on this side of the Shroud since the Dark Ages. Influencing the Hecata towards such behaviour. Very human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 12-16-2022, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:12:06-08:00","id":1499884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499880#post1499880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are only accidentally evil by human standards. They have been classically an example of blue and orange morality, creatures of deep, alien spirituality. I think the Giovanni were kept because they are a very human kind of evil. They are people who can be played up as often having three or four humanity rather than eight in Honorable Accord or Path of the Feral Heart or whathaveyou. The Giovanni are evil in a way that still keeps Humanity central. So they get to stay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that applies to 2nd Edition Sabbat but it didn't apply to 1st Edition Sabbat (0 Humanity), who literally had Satanists compromising a large portion of their number (and not Levayian) or Revised who had Sabbat state that they were EVIL not amoral and directly against God as well as morality.<br /> <br /> Reflected by most being Low Humanity rather than Path followers.<br /> <br /> Which is to say the alien amoral Sabbat have always been more a fan creation than a canonical interpretation. Which I, should clarify, I think is stupid. The alien ones are more interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:12:56-08:00","id":1499885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499881#post1499881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the Sabbat that got them labeled as &quot;not fitting the themes of the edition&quot;, as I understand it, is that they eschew humanity and embrace their vampiric nature. But again <i>they kept the Setites</i>. The other cult that sees their vampirism as the gift of getting the blood of a god in their veins so that they can destroy every semblance of functioning human society to free everybody from the chains of the aeons. Path of Typhon/Path of Sutekh, Path of Ecstasy... they're more invested in the &quot;well-being&quot; of humans than the Sabbat, but not exactly humanity types. They're basically blood sucking snake demons, and they are fine with that.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Hecata, and the Giovanni have the mortal evil and humanity nailed, but the Harbingers? Path of Death and the Soul. Human lives are meaningless and so are emotional attachments, we're just here to study and record the data of your various horrible deaths. Spent a thousand years going insane in purgatory/hell and haven't really been significantly established on this side of the Shroud since the Dark Ages. Influencing the Hecata towards such behaviour. Very human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't get the idea that the Fifth Edition is meant to be more moral and kind.<br /> <br /> The books are very clear vampires are scum.<br /> <br /> More than any previous edition, including Revised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:28:13-08:00","id":1499889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499885#post1499885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't get the idea that the Fifth Edition is meant to be more moral and kind.<br /> <br /> The books are very clear vampires are scum.<br /> <br /> More than any previous edition, including Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I blame the descriptions of the humanity stages and the no Sabbat, personally. I also find that V5 goes so hard on &quot;vampires BAD&quot; that I'm further inclined to play Superheroes with Fangs out of irritation. (How can I have a nuanced exploration of morality, desperation and evil when the horse has been beaten to death so hard its corpse is glue?)<br /> <br /> I just really don't get how <i>these</i> cults of inhuman bastards are fine (Bahari, Setite, Hecata), but <i>that</i> cult of inhuman bastards is badwrongfun.<br /> The only difference I can see is that of all vampires, the Sabbat are the least connected to humanity. Setites and Bahari have their cults and teachings they bestow to humans, while Sabbat truly embrace the meaning of the word <i>kine</i>. How many people who enjoy beef take an interest in the lives of cows? Which leads back to the idea that the point of V5 is that it's a game focused on obsessing over humans and humanity in some fashion, and other play styles are wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 12-16-2022, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:44:19-08:00","id":1499895,"title":"","content":"Double post delete please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:51:55-08:00","id":1499900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499889#post1499889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I blame the descriptions of the humanity stages and the no Sabbat, personally. I also find that V5 goes so hard on &quot;vampires BAD&quot; that I'm further inclined to play Superheroes with Fangs out of irritation. (How can I have a nuanced exploration of morality, desperation and evil when the horse has been beaten to death so hard its corpse is glue?)<br /> <br /> I just really don't get how <i>these</i> cults of inhuman bastards are fine (Bahari, Setite, Hecata), but <i>that</i> cult of inhuman bastards is badwrongfun.<br /> The only difference I can see is that of all vampires, the Sabbat are the least connected to humanity. Setites and Bahari have their cults and teachings they bestow to humans, while Sabbat truly embrace the meaning of the word <i>kine</i>. How many people who enjoy beef take an interest in the lives of cows? Which leads back to the idea that the point of V5 is that it's a game focused on obsessing over humans and humanity in some fashion, and other play styles are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to work on the assumption the Sabbats absence either being corporate mandated, pretty much every arguement I've heard against them being played is bad and if I've clocked that then I'm sure the people working for then have<br /> <br /> The paths absence is more of a mystery. I suppose they might be sincere about the trying to stay true to a vision but that implies a lack of self awareness and theory of mind.<br /> <br /> My main theory is they're afraid people won't want to play an early low level neonate anarch if you bring back all the old toys which seems to miss the forest for the trees about early unlife neonate anarch games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-16-2022, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T03:28:54-08:00","id":1499937,"title":"","content":"V5's Sabbat is a really poor attempt to copy what Onyx Path did with Belial's Brood.<br /> <br /> Wow, another 'V5 is Requiem' complaint. Yes, it's the main thing I dislike about it. Buyback to BB.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood were intentionally introduced as a throwback to 1e Sabbat, satanic vampires who revel in being evil. They were also the easy bad guy because acting like that is, to put it simply, stupid and so most members of the Brood were going to be low BP Neonates. Then the writers decided to add depth and they became the 2e Sabbat, more philosophical than alien but. With that mixture of legitimacy and hipocracy. You could actually play a full Brood chronicle, and it could have just as much variety as one starring the core Covenants.<br /> <br /> Then Requiem 2e came out, and the Brood weren't there. They were just gone because the focus was elsewhere. Even Secrets of the Covenants didn't say anything. But when they did appear the new version was awesome, removing the hipocracy, flipping them from being doomed to eventual Draugrhood to being Draugr who had developed minds, and just bleed awesome. They made me really want to run a Belial's Brood chronicle, and ideally get a full book on this new version. They might have lost some stuff, but they gained for everything they lost.<br /> <br /> V5 Sabbat meanwhile just lost. Lost their space in the core, lost some of their traits to the Anarchs, lost their interesting alien members. It would be as if the Brood had returned as satanic anarchists who tend to die young.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T09:21:18-08:00","id":1499948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499885#post1499885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't get the idea that the Fifth Edition is meant to be more moral and kind.<br /> <br /> The books are very clear vampires are scum.<br /> <br /> More than any previous edition, including Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't you say that the fact - derived from 1th Edition through Revised and still developed and described in V20 - that there are Kindred who are to at least a moderate, but significant, extent friendly, positive, ambitious, hopeful, optimistic, and reasonable - and who can realize personal and group / team objectives and goals - still applies in V5, included in at least in some of this edition's books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T09:26:54-08:00","id":1499949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499948#post1499948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't you say that the fact - derived from 1th Edition through Revised and still developed and described in V20 - that there are Kindred who are to at least a moderate, but significant, extent friendly, positive, ambitious, hopeful, optimistic, and reasonable - and who can realize personal and group / team objectives and goals - still applies in V5, included in at least in some of this edition's books?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's interesting to note that the books have generally taken a much more &quot;darker and grittier&quot; approach with each Edition and somewhat to the books' discomfort. Fifth Edition seems determined to make every vampire heavily focused on Frenzy, The Beast, and likely to have flipped out and hurt SOMEONE innocent at some point in their past.<br /> <br /> I think you can certainly play a &quot;good&quot; guy in that LA by Night downplays this severely.<br /> <br /> Ditto some other spin offs.<br /> <br /> But it's interesting that when WINTER TIDE was reviewed by Vampire Reviews they commented on how 5th Edition was THE DARKEST DARK DEPRESSING DARK THAT EVER DARKED.<br /> <br /> Which was an interesting outsider's perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T09:58:26-08:00","id":1499953,"title":"","content":"For me a stickler is that pre-V5, Vampires <i>as a whole</i> were bad but that was entirely the product of how they chose to deal with their difficult circumstances. In v5 all vampires are bad because they choose not to kill themselves because that's the only good thing they can do. The more vampire (potent) they are, the worse they are, and the more human they are the better. Your first and last mistake should be getting embraced.<br /> That's neither fun nor compelling nor relatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T10:01:31-08:00","id":1499954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499953#post1499953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me a stickler is that pre-V5, Vampires <i>as a whole</i> were bad but that was entirely the product of how they chose to deal with their difficult circumstances. In v5 all vampires are bad because they choose not to kill themselves because that's the only good thing they can do. The more vampire (potent) they are, the worse they are, and the more human they are the better. Your first and last mistake should be getting embraced.<br /> That's neither fun nor compelling nor relatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, flat out Pre-V5 made it absolutely clear you were a monster even then. That was the point. Being a vampire was about being a BAD guy and you WOULD kill at least a couple of innocents through the existing rules.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T21:41:04-08:00","id":1500007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499873#post1499873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ministry, Banu Haqim, and Hecata are now all playable fucked-up factions.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's the incredibly fucked up and weird Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are now unplayable.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are still knee capped by humanity and Touchstones. Blood cults are neutered by them as well. I read Blood Gods and thought 'thats it? That's the all?'<br /> <br /> Tho hunger dice do require you to kill multiple people a night to avoid masquerade breaking messy/bestial rolls, so I suppose that is darker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-18-2022, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T21:54:13-08:00","id":1500008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500007#post1500007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are still knee capped by humanity and Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can go into some sick places with Touchstones but I think Touchstones are a stupid rule.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T23:59:16-08:00","id":1500015,"title":"","content":"Vampires need mortals to survive: you cannot totally distance you from them, even when justifying evil choices. <br /> <br /> That those Vampires who thought themselves a different and superior species were deluded, was already implied when they canonized that Paths were a bastard version of Roads, aimed at providing cohesion to the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> Making it so central and evident was bound to be controversial, but if one is willing to engage with the system, the Convinction-Tenets-Touchstone trio still gives you huge flexibility. <br /> <br /> As for how dark were, and how much you were supposed to be a killer, fluff implied you would have snapped and killed: perhaps rules didn't support it as much, but I do distinctly remember Clanbook Toreador Revised speaking of the fact that eventually you would awake with pieces of liver on your face. <br /> <br /> Going to the Sabbat topic: complaints here are well more grounded. I like the general idea behind the new Sabbat (medieval death cult was always my fav), the book is good for providing Antagonist ideas and using them in your Chronicle, but not engaging with the past plot seeds of the implied Sabbat fall, I feel it was definitely a weakness. <br /> <br /> Working more on it would have justified more the rise of the Anarchs, and provided a more organic evolution towards the new metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T00:39:10-08:00","id":1500017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500015#post1500015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(medieval death cult was always my fav), .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm really sorry to quibble but what exactly is a medieval death cult? I've hear this phrase heavily used as point of referance but medieval people didn't really have death cults, the closest equivelant being flaggelants who explicitly don't want to die and the hashashin who are more a warrior order.<br /> <br /> Death cults doesn't even appear to be a thing outside as a descriptor for suicide cults or mortuary cults both of which are nothing like the sabbat . I know I'm being finicky here but im a history nerd It's like a stone in my shoe whenever I hear it since it's a slogan thrown around about the Sabbat and the only other place it's generally used is warhammer 40.000 about pvc ninjas<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500015#post1500015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working more on it would have justified more the rise of the Anarchs, and provided a more organic evolution towards the new metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The tricky part is the devolution of the Sabbat is ultimatly pointless in praxis. Since you can't play them the only interaction is hostile. On a practical level a carmarilla neonate from revised vs v5 won't actually experiance any actual difference in their interactions and an anarch only very slight variations if somehow they're in a situation with prolonged non hostile exposure.<br /> <br /> Nothing was gained only denied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-18-2022, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T00:56:10-08:00","id":1500021,"title":"","content":"Double post delete pls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T05:20:18-08:00","id":1500029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500008#post1500008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you can go into some sick places with Touchstones but I think Touchstones are a stupid rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You totally can, but 1) that starts to look a lot like an abusive relationship, which can be too much RL in the the setting for certain players, and 2) It's still showing some kind of link to humans, which is flat out against the point of some Paths/Cults...like Death and the Soul doesn't care about tonights experiment as a sentient being, it's a thing to be used to sate curiosity, nothing more, Ministry shouldn't care about the target, it's a soul to corrupt, destroy, and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T05:35:10-08:00","id":1500030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1499954#post1499954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, flat out Pre-V5 made it absolutely clear you were a monster even then. That was the point. Being a vampire was about being a BAD guy and you WOULD kill at least a couple of innocents through the existing rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I'm not really sure why you don't understand. Pre-V5 vampires were physically monsters and had a monsterous society but they were quite capable of being good people and doing no harm, or at least being a net positive on the community. Like Frankenstein's monster wasn't really a monster, and Vampires of 1e could control themselves and limit the damage they do to benign levels. Hell vampires in 1st ed had a reasonable window towards actually becoming human again. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V5? Like, you can't reasonably avoid messy criticals (killing people isn't reasonable) so you shouldn't really like, ever enter the company of people. Being a vampire is all shit for you and shit for everyone around you and even if you do your best you're still toxic. That might do well to capture how some people feel about themselves but it's not fun to base a game around. IIRC that window to regain your humanity is still gone, so really the only good thing you can do is self destruct, maybe taking out some other vampires with you. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T09:19:05-08:00","id":1500044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500029#post1500029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You totally can, but 1) that starts to look a lot like an abusive relationship, which can be too much RL in the the setting for certain players, and 2) It's still showing some kind of link to humans, which is flat out against the point of some Paths/Cults...like Death and the Soul doesn't care about tonights experiment as a sentient being, it's a thing to be used to sate curiosity, nothing more, Ministry shouldn't care about the target, it's a soul to corrupt, destroy, and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is probably why Talley and others don't have Touchstones.<br /> <br /> V5 seems to have hit on the awkward compromise that Paths exist but they're for NPCs only despite a much more flexible humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T09:21:08-08:00","id":1500045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500030#post1500030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I'm not really sure why you don't understand. Pre-V5 vampires were physically monsters and had a monsterous society but they were quite capable of being good people and doing no harm, or at least being a net positive on the community. Like Frankenstein's monster wasn't really a monster, and Vampires of 1e could control themselves and limit the damage they do to benign levels. Hell vampires in 1st ed had a reasonable window towards actually becoming human again. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V5? Like, you can't reasonably avoid messy criticals (killing people isn't reasonable) so you shouldn't really like, ever enter the company of people. Being a vampire is all shit for you and shit for everyone around you and even if you do your best you're still toxic. That might do well to capture how some people feel about themselves but it's not fun to base a game around. IIRC that window to regain your humanity is still gone, so really the only good thing you can do is self destruct, maybe taking out some other vampires with you. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You're saying I don't understand but I'm saying I disagree. Frankly, I think the rules did not remotely allow you to be a &quot;good&quot; vampire if you followed them and that even a Good-Ish vampire still had monstrous urges for frenzy and hunger for blood that would make them evil-ish.<br /> <br /> It was always the point of the game from 1st Edition onward.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T09:42:12-08:00","id":1500050,"title":"","content":"1e? Absolutely not. You can totally play a &quot;friendly neighbourhood vampire&quot;. You can feed without harming people and it's quite easy to avoid frenzy if you're smart and keep yourself well fed and out of stressful situations. You can bring a positive effect on the human community with your many lifetimes of expertise. <br /> <br /> Most vampire problems, not including rookie mistakes, stem from either struggling to compete with other vampires or being a bad person in general, rather than anything to do with the innate status of &quot;Being a vampire&quot;. You can totally learn how feed safely, you can totally learn to avoid frenzies, you can totally learn to protect your secret without causing problems. V5 vampires can't learn these things because their hunger functions differently and they're constantly going to be nervous wrecks that might overkill anything more than a simple task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T10:12:47-08:00","id":1500054,"title":"","content":"A friend of mind is playing with idea of running v5 as early neonate and then shifting to v20 at late neonate. I think it has potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T13:19:03-08:00","id":1500066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500017#post1500017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm really sorry to quibble but what exactly is a medieval death cult? I've hear this phrase heavily used as point of referance but medieval people didn't really have death cults, the closest equivelant being flaggelants who explicitly don't want to die and the hashashin who are more a warrior order.<br /> <br /> Death cults doesn't even appear to be a thing outside as a descriptor for suicide cults or mortuary cults both of which are nothing like the sabbat . I know I'm being finicky here but im a history nerd It's like a stone in my shoe whenever I hear it since it's a slogan thrown around about the Sabbat and the only other place it's generally used is warhammer 40.000 about pvc ninjas<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The tricky part is the devolution of the Sabbat is ultimatly pointless in praxis. Since you can't play them the only interaction is hostile. On a practical level a carmarilla neonate from revised won't actually experiance any actual difference in their interactions and an anarch only very slight variations if somehow they're in a situation with prolonged non hostile exposure.<br /> <br /> Nothing was gained only denied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that description always annoyed me as well. The Sabbat is more an alliance of different religions, none of them death cults except Death and the Soul. By and large, it's an alliance of disparate religions joined by the common goal of surviving the Antedeluvians, and those rival political factions that would kill them for favoring various religious devotions over sire, clan, and feudalism. Effectively, it's as if those knights who wanted to follow the Pope went to war with those knights who wanted to follow the King.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T00:55:38-08:00","id":1500086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500050#post1500050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e? Absolutely not. You can totally play a &quot;friendly neighbourhood vampire&quot;. You can feed without harming people and it's quite easy to avoid frenzy if you're smart and keep yourself well fed and out of stressful situations. You can bring a positive effect on the human community with your many lifetimes of expertise.<br /> <br /> Most vampire problems, not including rookie mistakes, stem from either struggling to compete with other vampires or being a bad person in general, rather than anything to do with the innate status of &quot;Being a vampire&quot;. You can totally learn how feed safely, you can totally learn to avoid frenzies, you can totally learn to protect your secret without causing problems. V5 vampires can't learn these things because their hunger functions differently and they're constantly going to be nervous wrecks that might overkill anything more than a simple task.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a drastic misrepresentation of 1st Edition and really undercuts a lot of what made the game revolutionary at the time. Previously, the player characters were all meant to be monster hunters either of the D&amp;D or Call of Cthulhu or Cyberpunk kind. What made V:TM so awesome at the time was that YOU were the monster. Yes, you COULD be a superhero with fangs but that was coming with the caveat of the Beast and Hunger. I think you dramatically overstate just how easy it was to avoid that if you were enforcing the rules as written as you could easily go through a lot of blood in a very quick amount of time using your Disciplines.<br /> <br /> And unless you DID have Self-Control 5, you would definitely frenzy and kill someone and even then the dice could always botch and trip you up.<br /> <br /> The game is all about the melancholy of being a vampire and the whole &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; business that encouraged you to try to resist the Beast, be an Anarch, and be LESS of a monster than the Elders (or worse, Sabbat). That didn't mean you weren't a monster, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500066#post1500066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that description always annoyed me as well. The Sabbat is more an alliance of different religions, none of them death cults except Death and the Soul. By and large, it's an alliance of disparate religions joined by the common goal of surviving the Antedeluvians, and those rival political factions that would kill them for favoring various religious devotions over sire, clan, and feudalism. Effectively, it's as if those knights who wanted to follow the Pope went to war with those knights who wanted to follow the King.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, I disagree.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are a Medieval death cult in literal terms first of all. Because they are a A:] A Cult. B:] Founded in the Middle Ages. C:] Worship the state of vampirism, which is the status of undeath as well as Caine as their Anti-Christ/God figure. But less literally, I think it largely depends on how sincerely you buy what the Sabbat is selling. Because the Sabbat exists on two levels and it's why I love them as a group second only to the Anarchs (who have the same problem).<br /> <br /> 1:] <b>Level One</b>: The Sabbat is a erudite philosophical organization of competing Kindred religions and philosophies under one single umbrella religion of shared Caine worship. It exists to explore the extremes of the vampire experience as well as provide you unlimited freedom from the Masquerade or chaining the Beast.<br /> <br /> 2:] <b>Level Two</b>: None of this actually applies to you. You are a Blood Bound slave to the Bishops and you will die pointlessly as cannon fodder in a never-ending war for more territory. It is a scam.<br /> <br /> Now here's the the thing about 2, the Sabbat will tell you that if you're strong, clever, and superior then you will move from Level 2 to Level 1. However, it's essentially capitalism in a Punk setting. No, you will not. The odds are astronomical and the chances of you doing so are basically dumb luck.<br /> <br /> You can survive and move up in the cult, just as the same as you could, I dunno, rise up in any cult.<br /> <br /> However, ironically, the best way to do so is probably to be as backstabbing and disloyal as possible and you have to do that against magical blood slavery and more traditional indoctrination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-19-2022, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T01:34:43-08:00","id":1500088,"title":"","content":"Neither of those are really match the descriptor death cult. I'm not even convinced the Sabbat is a cult in the sense we use the word. The whole thing sounds like slogans to rationalize Sabbat as unplayable or downplay the moral ambiguities of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Fun fact the Sabbat were founded in 1493 so it's debatable if they're even medieval and not early modern. Depending on wear you wrap up that period (my preffered choice is 1454, with the fall of constantinople). I suppose &quot;early modern death cult&quot; doesn't have the same ring to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-19-2022, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T04:00:31-08:00","id":1500091,"title":"","content":"Death cult? I thought the Sabbat were more like appropriated Wan Kuei, retroactively speaking. Accepting what you are now, trying to shape yourself up to something resembling an ethical person, focus on communities, experience with spirits and demons\u2026<br /> <br /> In fact the table-canon I\u2019ve been running with Cainite and Wan Kuei interaction is that the Sabbat is responsible for the animus; the Wan Kuei know of the \u2018barbarians\u2019 as thieves and mockeries of their holy teachings, while non-Sabbat Cainites know of the \u2018cathayans\u2019 as the origin of the Sabbat. While Sabbat members generally don\u2019t give a damn to either. <br /> <br /> So basically, the Sabbat as a cargo cult (ideological cargo cult? inverse cargo cult?) plus doomsday cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 12-19-2022, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T06:23:47-08:00","id":1500094,"title":"","content":"I always saw them more as a militataristic constitutional monarchy with theocratic elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T09:40:46-08:00","id":1500100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500088#post1500088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of those are really match the descriptor death cult. I'm not even convinced the Sabbat is a cult in the sense we use the word. The whole thing sounds like slogans to rationalize Sabbat as unplayable or downplay the moral ambiguities of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Fun fact the Sabbat were founded in 1493 so it's debatable if they're even medieval and not early modern. Depending on wear you wrap up that period (my preffered choice is 1454, with the fall of constantinople). I suppose &quot;early modern death cult&quot; doesn't have the same ring to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Sabbat are a cult in that it is a religious society that attempts to completely isolate the majority of is members and control all of their behavior and belief.<br /> <br /> And while 1493 is when the Sabbat officially began, the organization's roots are in the First Anarch Revolt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T09:55:55-08:00","id":1500102,"title":"","content":"Fun fact, the Camarilla's roots are also in the first Anarch revolt, it's basically responsible for completely restructuring European kindred society, including the Brujah falling from being a High Clan to Rabble. The Sabbat's beliefs may be from the Medieval period or may be older, it depends on if you assume the Caine myth is true (which it is canonically, but it's still likely that the commonly known version is distorted). But that's probably just an extension of the cWoD being Americentric and Eurocentric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T10:51:56-08:00","id":1500106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500100#post1500100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Sabbat are a cult in that it is a religious society that attempts to completely isolate the majority of is members and control all of their behavior and belief.<br /> <br /> And while 1493 is when the Sabbat officially began, the organization's roots are in the First Anarch Revolt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sabbats capacity or inclination to control its followers is actually pretty limited. it had cultural trends and norms but either allow large degree of deviance or is unable to enforce the level of control typical of cults. This shows in its major problem with infernalism, factionalism and groups which strongly deviate from 'ideal'.<br /> <br /> You could probably argue that the lower levels are cultish with indoctrination and exploitation but it doesn't really act like a cult collectively, by its nature and intent it cant act like a cult. Realistically how are you even going to enforce cult control over groups like the nomad packs, unified bloodlines, sub groups or the two primary clans?<br /> <br /> So the first anarch revolt was a medieval death cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-19-2022, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T12:01:31-08:00","id":1500115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500100#post1500100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Sabbat are a cult in that it is a religious society that attempts to completely isolate the majority of is members and control all of their behavior and belief.<br /> <br /> And while 1493 is when the Sabbat officially began, the organization's roots are in the First Anarch Revolt.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> It could be considered alternatively that clearly often the more radical, stark, dark, vibrant, and vehement of the very beliefs, methods, philosophies, ideas, viewpoints, and outlooks for which Sabbat is most known (and which often provide Sabbat Vampires with various benefits, interesting situations, and gains) can be disregarded to various extents (which can be relatively slight at times, but still should be considered meaningful and significant) under some of the laws and rules held by Sword of Caine, and certainly by members participating in some of the Sabbat factions organizations. The more general / overall Sabbat methodfs, outlooks, beliefs, and ideas can also be put to the side when events, choices, and matters are resolved under considerations involving teams, social networks, and task groups who follow the various methods, laws, rules, and concepts, and also philosophies of the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> (And perhaps also, more rarely, the Roads from Vampire: Dark Ages. Does anyone have any sure / certain information in regard to this?)<br /> <br /> Also, the viewpoints, concepts, rules, and philosophies related to the particular Sabbat Clans and Sabbat Bloodlines (among my favourite are the Tremere Antitribu, the Toreador Antitribu, and Brujah Antitribu) may very well take precedence and be more important in regard to many situations and decisions / choices, compared to the distinctly / clearly universal and overall rules, outlooks methods, and ideas held by the Sabbat Vampires, Revenants involved with the Sabbat, and Sabbat Ghouls. And possibly also by some of the various Nightfolk (or supernatural / otherwordly / magical citizens \\ beings \\ persons) who might be allies, supporters, lovers, friends, and\\or supporters of the Deathless / Vampiric supernatural persons from the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I do wonder whether each of the four Revenant families who are involved extensively with the Sabbat Vampires have preferred or favourite Clans or Clan-similar Bloodlines who they consider outright easier or nicer to cooperate, party, plot, and deal with. The Zantosa Revenants could be considered to be more easily invovled with the Toreador Antitribu or the Serpents of Light, but both of these choices are rather stereotypical, simple, or straightforward. What about the Obertus Revenants, the Grimaldi Revenants, and Bratovitch Revenants in regard to this topic / question / matter / issue ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T12:21:32-08:00","id":1500116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500086#post1500086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That didn't mean you weren't a monster, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, to look at it another way, just because you're a monster doesn't mean you can't do good.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, vampires are monstrous.<br /> <br /> All things that live (or &quot;live&quot; in their case) want to live and avoid suffering. The price for this is the death and suffering of others. Creation can not be initiated or sustained without destruction. You cannot exist without the sacrifices of others. Your house is built of dead trees and minerals torn from the Earth (destroying habitat in its wake), warmed by the death of primordial beasts, when you got that house many others did not, it's paid for with a job that you got and so others didn't, you may feed on meat gained from the death of animals and even if not the death of animals was required at some point to grow the plant matter you eat. Animals, plants and human labor are exploited for you to live your life. The food chain demands death or the world collapses. Atoms strip each other of electrons. The universe cannibalises itself. Even if other life forms don't matter to you (which is how we got into the current climate mess) your existence will still lead to some degree of deprivation and suffering for other humans, somewhere. You were forged from history, which is a fucking hellhole.<br /> <br /> To exist is a monstrous act that brings suffering, harm and death to others. Nature is monstrous. We don't even need vampires, the stuff that actually exists is a fucking horror-show. But what are you supposed to do? Your own suffering and death doesn't actually change anything, in the end. You can decide &quot;that's just how it is&quot; and not care, you can develop standards by which you decide which lives are less important (deserve to suffer more than) others, you can look for ways to minimize the damage you do while you seek a better way forward.<br /> <br /> And this feeds into ethics, philosophy, religion and the cycles of conflict and misery that come from it. People have long looked at the world and each other, and themselves and asked &quot;why are we so fucked up?&quot; &quot;what can we do to stop this?&quot; &quot;is there a way?&quot; &quot;is there even any point?&quot;<br /> And so comes dharma, original sin and redemption, the illusions of desire and escape of enlightenment, the laws of God by which one should live to live a life that benefits you and the world, fascism, communism, Social Darwinism, so on so forth.<br /> <br /> Vampires all have ideas about how to cope with what they are, why they are, what to do about it, on levels both individual and as collectives, and conflict arises from it.<br /> <br /> To me that's the core of vampires. Exploring monstrosity through exaggeration. Our own monstrosity, the monstrosity built into a fundamentally awful (yet beautiful) universe, and how we cope and what it makes us into. A one note &quot;Vampire BAD WRONG EVUUUL,&quot; cheapens the whole experience. The idea that vampires should kill themselves drives me up the wall, and frankly feels like... victim blaming, for lack of a better word. You got murdered? Defiled forever, abomination, kys. <i>Lovely.</i> &quot;Even if you do good things, they don't matter because you're a monster&quot; means there's no reason to give a damn at all. A vampire is still a person, a vampire still experiences suffering. If you don't value a person's right to exist and avoid suffering, you shouldn't be surprised that they don't give a damn about you. Goes in both ways, for kindred and mortals.<br /> <br /> Good and evil are ultimately what you do. A vampire is a monster, yeah. They're not good, their motivations don't even need to be good, but they can <i>do</i> good. The Toreador who has a flourishing domain that is perfectly clear of litter and is a sanctuary for nature in the urban jungle because they find it aesthetically pleasing, has done good. Vampires who push for eco policies, and against wars, or just to make life better to live because they fucking live here (and will be here to deal with the fallout for centuries longer then us) are doing good. The people who live in the Koldun's domain are grateful not to live with the threat of extortion rackets, or dying in a drive by or a gang war, even if it's because the holder is a territorial nutcase who likes a tidy domain.<br /> <br /> Exploring this and coming to your own opinions is far more interesting than having EVIL printed in all caps fifteen times a page (exaggeration, but that's what it feels like. Not just in V5, this annoyed me in previous editions too. I got it in the first page, I'm literate and capable of critical thinking, you don't need to keep fuckin' telling me!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 12-19-2022, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T23:07:07-08:00","id":1500166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500086#post1500086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is a drastic misrepresentation of 1st Edition and really undercuts a lot of what made the game revolutionary at the time. Previously, the player characters were all meant to be monster hunters either of the D&amp;D or Call of Cthulhu or Cyberpunk kind. What made V:TM so awesome at the time was that YOU were the monster. Yes, you COULD be a superhero with fangs but that was coming with the caveat of the Beast and Hunger. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The game is all about the melancholy of being a vampire and the whole &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; business that encouraged you to try to resist the Beast, be an Anarch, and be LESS of a monster than the Elders (or worse, Sabbat). That didn't mean you weren't a monster, though.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Or it was capitalist satire. Your milage may vary, but as soon as most players get into vampire they start trying to get rich. It's all about money, status, power. They get greedy and want to devour elders (even though they don't have a single attribute at 5 waiting to get to 6). Most of the &quot;oh it sucks to be a vampire&quot; seems like Torador melodrama, because mechanically the only real downers concern sleeping for the majority of the day and the fact that people older and more powerful than you are likely to object to your power grabbing natures. That obscene drive for riches made players monsters far more quickly than the Beast ever could. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think you dramatically overstate just how easy it was to avoid that if you were enforcing the rules as written as you could easily go through a lot of blood in a very quick amount of time using your Disciplines.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> If you were enforcing the rules as written then you'd know what a load you've just spouted. I'm aware your playstyle is more anarch splatterpunk than methodical masterminds but even then you're not going to be frenzying much. <br /> 1: you shouldn't be needing disciplines much if you're any good at the game. Disciplines are there to make unlife easier, not a crutch you need to depend on. <br /> 2: It might've been different from 1e, but most common disciplines before V5 didn't use blood. Dominate? entirely Free. Obfuscate? Free except when you want to raise appearance. Auspex? Free. Potence? Free. Only presence, celerity and the path-side of thaumaturgy used a significant amount of blood. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Yes, getting insulted can be a frenzy check, but if you're half-decent with people you're not going to be insulted much. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T00:03:55-08:00","id":1500167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500116#post1500116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, to look at it another way, just because you're a monster doesn't mean you can't do good.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, vampires are monstrous.<br /> <br /> All things that live (or &amp;quot;live&amp;quot; in their case) want to live and avoid suffering. The price for this is the death and suffering of others. Creation can not be initiated or sustained without destruction. You cannot exist without the sacrifices of others. Your house is built of dead trees and minerals torn from the Earth (destroying habitat in its wake), warmed by the death of primordial beasts, when you got that house many others did not, it's paid for with a job that you got and so others didn't, you may feed on meat gained from the death of animals and even if not the death of animals was required at some point to grow the plant matter you eat. Animals, plants and human labor are exploited for you to live your life. The food chain demands death or the world collapses. Atoms strip each other of electrons. The universe cannibalises itself. Even if other life forms don't matter to you (which is how we got into the current climate mess) your existence will still lead to some degree of deprivation and suffering for other humans, somewhere. You were forged from history, which is a fucking hellhole.<br /> <br /> To exist is a monstrous act that brings suffering, harm and death to others. Nature is monstrous. We don't even need vampires, the stuff that actually exists is a fucking horror-show. But what are you supposed to do? Your own suffering and death doesn't actually change anything, in the end. You can decide &amp;quot;that's just how it is&amp;quot; and not care, you can develop standards by which you decide which lives are less important (deserve to suffer more than) others, you can look for ways to minimize the damage you do while you seek a better way forward.<br /> <br /> And this feeds into ethics, philosophy, religion and the cycles of conflict and misery that come from it. People have long looked at the world and each other, and themselves and asked &amp;quot;why are we so fucked up?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;what can we do to stop this?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;is there a way?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;is there even any point?&amp;quot;<br /> And so comes dharma, original sin and redemption, the illusions of desire and escape of enlightenment, the laws of God by which one should live to live a life that benefits you and the world, fascism, communism, Social Darwinism, so on so forth.<br /> <br /> Vampires all have ideas about how to cope with what they are, why they are, what to do about it, on levels both individual and as collectives, and conflict arises from it.<br /> <br /> To me that's the core of vampires. Exploring monstrosity through exaggeration. Our own monstrosity, the monstrosity built into a fundamentally awful (yet beautiful) universe, and how we cope and what it makes us into. A one note &amp;quot;Vampire BAD WRONG EVUUUL,&amp;quot; cheapens the whole experience. The idea that vampires should kill themselves drives me up the wall, and frankly feels like... victim blaming, for lack of a better word. You got murdered? Defiled forever, abomination, kys. <i>Lovely.</i> &amp;quot;Even if you do good things, they don't matter because you're a monster&amp;quot; means there's no reason to give a damn at all. A vampire is still a person, a vampire still experiences suffering. If you don't value a person's right to exist and avoid suffering, you shouldn't be surprised that they don't give a damn about you. Goes in both ways, for kindred and mortals.<br /> <br /> Good and evil are ultimately what you do. A vampire is a monster, yeah. They're not good, their motivations don't even need to be good, but they can <i>do</i> good. The Toreador who has a flourishing domain that is perfectly clear of litter and is a sanctuary for nature in the urban jungle because they find it aesthetically pleasing, has done good. Vampires who push for eco policies, and against wars, or just to make life better to live because they fucking live here (and will be here to deal with the fallout for centuries longer then us) are doing good. The people who live in the Koldun's domain are grateful not to live with the threat of extortion rackets, or dying in a drive by or a gang war, even if it's because the holder is a territorial nutcase who likes a tidy domain.<br /> <br /> Exploring this and coming to your own opinions is far more interesting than having EVIL printed in all caps fifteen times a page (exaggeration, but that's what it feels like. Not just in V5, this annoyed me in previous editions too. I got it in the first page, I'm literate and capable of critical thinking, you don't need to keep fuckin' telling me!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me a lot of a conversation my current pc had when she was at the mercy of a high ranking mage. She touched on a lot of the points you comment on here. <br /> <br /> Her-&quot;I know I'm not human anymore but I'm still a person.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage-&quot;but are you a good person?&quot;<br /> <br /> Her-&quot;im as good as you can realistically be as a vampire. I think my good outweighs my bad.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T01:33:04-08:00","id":1500168,"title":"","content":"one blood a night + whatever lies you need to get it and stay safe isn't exactly monster material. If you're attractive, running a shelter, or materially incentivising people to be in your company you're probably doing them a favour. If owning a business and being well-off while doing little work is evil... well, like, that's something normal people do.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd argue a lot of people would appreciate ghouling while we're at it. Not growing old, staying in great physical condition, and experiencing<i> true love</i>? With a good domitor that's a bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-20-2022, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T02:12:57-08:00","id":1500169,"title":"","content":"A human who loses a blood point to a vampire and goes home with a slight case of anemia and hypotension is significantly better off than the unfortunate hen that went into my sandwich, or the sparrow I watched getting bludgeoned to death by a hungry gull this morning.<br /> <br /> You probably can't avoid accidents forever (even losing a little blood can be disastrous for me, so I'd make a shitty blood doll for any vampire that bit me not knowing that), and it's still not a safe or good thing you're doing for your donor/prey, and is a symptom of the fact that nature is pretty fundamentally exploitative and sick, but you can make your existence more ethical than most creatures can manage. More ethical feeding can be accomplished through consent, compensation, blood bags, etc. And many of the vampires who will survive to be ancilla will try to avoid a lot of killing. Aside from the practical side, a lot of vampiric ethical codes forbid wanton killing all over the place. They like an environment they can control, hunter activity all over the place and serial killers on the verge of wassail are not conductive to that.<br /> <br /> The fact that people are assholes, and vampiric society and, ironically, the demands of the masquerade, are your main moral problems in this approach.<br /> <br /> (I'm also of the opinion that while vampires being willing to harm us to sustain their existences is awful, and we're justified in defending ourselves, expecting people to either suffer horrific hunger until they weaken into a coma they can't wake from/die is pretty fucked up on our end too, and vampires are just as justified in prioritizing themselves as we are.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 12-20-2022, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T02:41:16-08:00","id":1500277,"title":"","content":"The way blood was handled was probably one of my favorite elements of V5. <br /> That is not to say the system is not without its faults, because it does have them. Some can easily be house ruled, others have been adjusted in the players guide supplement. <br /> The randomness of a rouse check is a bit annoying, but over long term it does even out, even though short bursts of bad luck are discouraging, the bursts of good luck are equally encouraging. <br /> I am not a huge messy criticals and bestial failures, but have found just to give a condition like the clan compulsions work splendidly, either overcome at the end of a session or when the session. A Messy critical with a computer roll may result in a Bane penalty to all rolls involving technology for the rest of the session as the beast no longer have patience for such things.<br /> <br /> I am not a fan of keeping Generation. The concept was fairly poor to start with, and more felt like a legacy product that needed to be kept. I could buy it if Generation was, much like we count human generations, an indication of when you were created, so thus even a 6th generation Kindred would create a 13th generation Child. Add some automatic thickening of the blood, so the generations automatically consolidate downwards. Blood potency solves a lot of issues. The tie-in with Generation is sort of neat, but it felt like something kept for its own sake, rather than something that actually brings something to the table.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is as someone has mentioned very powerful, but also exceedingly dangerous. One poor roll and Humanity is wiped. But a few good rolls and experience would skyrocketed. While I do like the idea, I think this could have been something they should have changed. Remove the power of it. For a lower generation/high blood potency, draining another vampire to death would be the only way to remove the last hunger. For younger Kindred, it would do nothing (more than fill their hunger, as if it was mortal). While this removes ones of the reasons why Elders fear the younger generations, just surviving a couple of centuries a monster would be ample to find unique reasons for the same paranoia. <br /> <br /> Hunting and feeding seems to be a goal. As has previously been mentioned, a lot of powers now risks the chance of Hunger, where as they in previous editions did not. From a mechanical standpoint, this makes the early (free) Disciplines more desirable. Something reliable that can be used on a nightly basis. It also puts the stakes higher when the higher level powers are used, because they are not used lightly. I have found this to be a good pacing in the game, the amount of disciplines used are a lot less and less relied on, instead I feel more players are thinking on their feet until they actually need to push something through, not because it is simple.<br /> <br /> V5 is more 'action'-oriented in the way it deals with a game session. There are higher chances of becoming hungry, something that was never really an issue in previous editions unless there was a fight basically. Now all sorts of actions drives this hunger. You can boost any attribute, making hunger relevant for any play style.<br /> Pre-V5, seen from a 13th generation vampire, you could, without risk for you or your prey, hunt every third night.<br /> In V5, there is a 12.5% chance that you are at 4 hunger by the third night (and a 12.5% that you are still at 1), with the average being 2 or 3. This is regardless of generation, some even have it harder, as their max hunger without killing is lower. This leads to a lot of questions about how the Masquerade could kept with these numbers, and I agree. There is a large difference between what is &quot;in-game time&quot; and what is &quot;out-of-game&quot; probabilities. <br /> Then once again, if you look how (my experience) of the game is, pre-V5 everyone would mostly use up blood doing something they wanted accomplished and hunt every night anyway to fill up. Sometimes several times. Botched hunts was not a per-session experience, but it came up a lot, in particular in Revised when it was just Perception + Herd, so there were a lot of 2-3 dice pools flying around (adopting the hunting rules from revised Dark Ages was done quickly by our groups). The same in V5, there is basically a hunt every session, but hunting in V5 is not only a job, it is also something that can add to your character in form of resonance and dyscrasias. <br /> <br /> Resonance and such a very addition, and adds a lot to the personal experience. Like everything else, there are things that could have been done better, thankfully it is also highly modular and easy to adjust or modulate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500168#post1500168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue a lot of people would appreciate ghouling while we're at it. Not growing old, staying in great physical condition, and experiencing<i> true love</i>? With a good domitor that's a bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>True love? The blood bond is the very opposite of true love. Sure, there are some perks like mentioned, but add to it an extreme addiction, obsession and obedience. Even if your domitor is &quot;good&quot;, it is still the sort of take all the money from their kids college funds to help their domitor out, even if said domitor would never ask for such a thing. It creates a life where basically everything centers around the needs of the domitor, someone who does in no way can feel the same way back. Holding employment is hard when all thoughts and concerns are on someone else, keeping friends and even family when all they want and need is to be around someone else. At the very best, it is what would be described as a very toxic relationship by any other standards, and that is with a &quot;good&quot; domitor.<br /> This is why Kindred influence is not based around ghouling, but leverage and exchange of favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T03:47:52-08:00","id":1500280,"title":"","content":"On reflection v5 is terms of how vampires function in feeding, the nasty dice and sustaining self is probably closer to Wraith than classic vtm. Thinking on it that's probably a better comparison than classic vs 5th","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-21-2022, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T05:46:24-08:00","id":1500288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500277#post1500277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True love? The blood bond is the very opposite of true love. Sure, there are some perks like mentioned, but add to it an extreme addiction, obsession and obedience. Even if your domitor is &quot;good&quot;, it is still the sort of take all the money from their kids college funds to help their domitor out, even if said domitor would never ask for such a thing. It creates a life where basically everything centers around the needs of the domitor, someone who does in no way can feel the same way back. Holding employment is hard when all thoughts and concerns are on someone else, keeping friends and even family when all they want and need is to be around someone else. At the very best, it is what would be described as a very toxic relationship by any other standards, and that is with a &quot;good&quot; domitor.<br /> This is why Kindred influence is not based around ghouling, but leverage and exchange of favors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Annoyingly the writing is vague enough, enough ST's like to make things difficult, and of course things must take the absolute worst possible interpretation because it's a horror game and you're not allowed to do things without suffering, that your interpretation is a popular one.<br /> <br /> Yes, <i>someone</i> might take money from the colledge fund to help the vampire out, even if said domitor would never ask for such a thing, but<br /> A: a good domitor should never appear to be in that kind of financial distress.<br /> B: a good domitor would likely invest back into their ghouls<br /> C: a good domitor ideally won't ghoul someone with so many attachments.<br /> D: Needing a substantial college fund is a sign that your country is backwards and... I digress.<br /> <br /> Holding employment? Like, no. That's not an issue. Either your domitor gives you your possition or if the lord is desperate you work day shifts with passion in the hopes of aiding your precious loved one.<br /> <br /> Addiction? If that's sated, it's not a problem.<br /> So with all problems out on the table easily solvable by half competent management, what's the issue? The ghoul gains a deep and profound sense of love. Is it rational? Love isn't. Will the ghoul occasionally be frustrated and do things they don't want to do? Try parenting. Kids can be incredibly difficult, but you feel indescribable joy when they succeed or become happy, and you feel acomplished when you give them that happiness, even if you had to be dragged through mud. The bond with a ghoul is <i>stronger</i> than the unconditional love a child gets, since it's much more difficult to tell a vampire that you're busy or that you'll do it later, but wouldn't the indescribable joy of aiding success be proportionately stronger? There's a lot of very lonely people in the world who feel their life is without meaning, imagine the psychological benefit of that level of attachment, just feeling happy knowing your loved one is nearby and that you make that person's life better? That's a sense of completion few people find.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T06:57:43-08:00","id":1500294,"title":"","content":"I've always found vtms attitude to ghouls a bit shit dark. Humanity rolls aside I'm unconvinced a vampire would want or need the ghoul around as much as the fluff implies. Realistically its in a vampires interest for them to live a pleasent life since it makes them easier to control carrot and stick.<br /> <br /> Tzmisce of coarse being the obvious acception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T08:04:01-08:00","id":1500297,"title":"","content":"I've honestly always assumed that, in practice, a ghoul's daytime errands don't take that long. Especially in Winter where days here last about 8 hours and kindred are a lot more active.<br /> <br /> Like, being a ghoul in Masquerade is a pretty shitty deal, and it's not much better in Requiem. But a competent ghoul is probably happy with it, as they'll likely have more leeway in how they complete their tasks and legitimate free time. It's a hard life, but an unending one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T09:09:07-08:00","id":1500302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1497012-feeding-in-classic-vampire-versus-v5?p=1500294#post1500294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always found vtms attitude to ghouls a bit shit dark. Humanity rolls aside I'm unconvinced a vampire would want or need the ghoul around as much as the fluff implies. Realistically its in a vampires interest for them to live a pleasent life since it makes them easier to control carrot and stick.<br /> <br /> Tzmisce of coarse being the obvious acception.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me I feel like there's a few narrators for the VtM describing what vampirism's like. In one corner you've got a melodramatic Toreador trying to create a mood and spreading tales of hyperbolic misery and in the other you've got a Nosferatu grounding things and offering reason, among other characters like the Tremere who only pops up in suplements and Brujah who doesn't understand the other side of the argument. The Nos's argument is pretty well backed by mechanics and how humans generally behave but the Toreador's flights of fancy are just so memorable that they shape opinions no matter how unreasonable, ephermal, or poorly supported by mechanics. Imagine 90% of the book suggests vampires are just people with a condition but when the Toreador pulls out the prose and says they're damned, soulless and static monsters people latch onto it, not really understanding that VTM heavily uses unreliable narrators/conflating VTM vampires with that other VTM IP they like. Like that one redacted study that says vaccines cause autism getting an unreasonable amount of traction when everything else says they shouldn't. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also<br /> I think Tzmisce are realistically going to be far better with the carrot and stick than most other clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T18:54:48-07:00","id":1520251,"title":"","content":"Well, a feeding that must be houseruled to work has several problems. Blood potency works wonderfully on Requiem, without generation and a clear first vampire. To the Maskerade it works poorly, because the game, even with some cool mechanics, punish the players for being ambitious and wanting to be stronger. Without that, the War of Ages makes no sense, and both Camarilla and Sabbath are severely defanged. Why create laws to protect something that has no benefits that overpass the drawbacks? Why cannibalize unworthy elders to be the Sword of Cain if it won't advance your goals? Street games are ok, but if I'm playing vampire is to be a vampire, not some angsty teen too afraid to access their gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}